ºÄ‚Ωä«°;ä$ªjµ’<\∞<ﬂıº~^)ªH ºˇs˛<}‰º£Âî<≥DsºßCvº⁄O”∫≠ ò<£Íœ<ç6=êA¸<tïû<áxÒª®Z¥<Ô€;tÊ[ª‹”G<Ãî=kÃì<ckÑªÁ8Ît≤º≠V<óÅW;Ö;;œ∂—<Ëà¬<Bâ¡º%ª<ÆÍ<˙ºÖ®z<°a <dÿ:Ω^L]<≤◊<= ␀=NC˜ºÍX9<yQ=-§ªﬁ£>ΩΩp>;Ωu˘<|é2ΩpŸ∑∫˚1ñº#é3ª∂ﬂ•<«Ö<•i	Ωõ=x5åºóÅW;¸ÍŒºÙâøº¬Â]:°≤]ºÕëºe›uºÍX9=dÿ:=€∑Œ;P¬0ΩÁ∏ÀªËç;ÑûÑºÄ‚º‰„<œ∂—<§é<i¸;⁄Jò∏°ΩÏ(0ª(OUπSbΩ º Fm=Pâ<õ⁄}7›ˆπ{"title": "REQUERIMIENTOS CAL\u00d3RICOS:The calculated caloric needs for the patient based on their ideal weight and activity level, determined to be 3091 kcal."}{"title": "MEDICINA DIGESTIVA:Medicina Digestiva is a medical department that manages digestive health and treatments."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULA PEPT\u00cdDICA HC/HP:F\u00f3rmula pept\u00eddica HC/HP is a specialized nutritional formula designed for patients with specific dietary needs."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULA POLIM\u00c9RICA HC/HP:F\u00f3rmula polim\u00e9rica HC/HP is a nutritional formula used for diabetic patients to manage their dietary intake."}{"title": "CONTROLES DE GLUCEMIA:Controles de glucemia are blood glucose monitoring tests conducted to assess the patient's blood sugar levels."}{"title": "CFTR:CFTR (Cystic Fibrosis Transmembrane Conductance Regulator) is the gene responsible for cystic fibrosis, coding for a chloride channel protein."}{"title": "MUTACI\u00d3N F508DEL:F508del is the most common mutation associated with cystic fibrosis, affecting the CFTR gene."}{"title": "INSUFICIENCIA PANCRE\u00c1TICA EXOCRINA:Exocrine pancreatic insufficiency (EPI) is a medical condition characterized by the pancreas's inability to produce sufficient digestive enzymes, which can lead to difficulties in digesting food properly. This condition is commonly associated with cystic fibrosis, where it significantly impacts the patient's ability to absorb nutrients effectively. Management of EPI often requires specific dietary adjustments to help mitigate the effects of the insufficient enzyme production and improve overall nutrient absorption."}{"title": "INSUFICIENCIA PANCRE\u00c1TICA ENDOCRINA:Endocrine pancreatic insufficiency is another complication of cystic fibrosis that can lead to diabetes."}{"title": "CONSULTAS EXTERNAS:\"CONSULTAS EXTERNAS\" refers to medical services that enable patients to receive care without the need for hospitalization. This includes medical follow-ups and assessments specifically for patients with cystic fibrosis, ensuring they receive the necessary attention and support in an outpatient setting."}{"title": "DRFQ:DRFQ refers to a specific type of diabetes diagnosed in patients, necessitating management and treatment strategies that include insulin administration and nutritional education. Additionally, it is associated with malnutrition related to cystic fibrosis, a condition that can worsen the prognosis of patients suffering from this genetic disorder. This highlights the importance of comprehensive care in managing both diabetes and the nutritional challenges faced by individuals with cystic fibrosis."}{"title": "SAMUEL:Samuel is a patient diagnosed with DRFQ at the age of 14, who has been undergoing treatment and management for his condition."}{"title": "INSULINA DEGLUDEC:Insulina degludec is a newer long-acting insulin used to improve glycemic control in patients with diabetes."}{"title": "EJERCICIO AER\u00d3BICO:Ejercicio aer\u00f3bico is a form of physical activity recommended for patients to improve their overall health and manage diabetes."}{"title": "MAL CONTROL GLUC\u00c9MICO:Mal control gluc\u00e9mico refers to the poor management of blood glucose levels in patients, which can lead to complications in diabetes."}{"title": "VITAMINAS LIPOSOLUBLES:VITAMINAS LIPOSOLUBLES, or fat-soluble vitamins, are essential nutrients that play a crucial role in various bodily functions. These vitamins, which include vitamins A, D, E, and K, are soluble in fats and oils, allowing them to be absorbed in the dietary fat consumed. In patients with cystic fibrosis (Fibrosis Qu\u00edstica), monitoring the intake of fat-soluble vitamins is particularly important due to malabsorption issues commonly associated with the condition. Additionally, the absorption of these vitamins may be further impacted by weight loss medications. Ensuring adequate levels of vitamins A, D, and E is vital for cystic fibrosis patients to prevent deficiencies and support their overall health."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULA POLIM\u00c9RICA HIPERCAL\u00d3RICA HIPERPROTEICA:A type of enteral nutrition formula that is hypercaloric and hyperproteic, specifically designed for diabetic patients."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULA POLIM\u00c9RICA NORMOCAL\u00d3RICA NORMOPROTEICA:"}{"title": "CYSTIC FIBROSIS:Cystic Fibrosis is a genetic disorder that significantly impacts the lungs and digestive system, resulting in severe respiratory and nutritional challenges for patients. This condition necessitates specialized nutritional care to manage the associated complications effectively."}{"title": "RIORDAN JR:Riordan JR is a researcher known for his work in identifying the cystic fibrosis gene and its implications."}{"title": "SOUTHERN KW:Southern KW is a researcher who conducted a survey of newborn screening for cystic fibrosis in Europe."}{"title": "FARRELL PM:Farrell PM is a researcher who studied the prevalence of cystic fibrosis in the European Union."}{"title": "BALLMANN M:Ballmann M is a researcher involved in clinical trials related to diabetes management in cystic fibrosis patients."}{"title": "HEPATOPAT\u00cdA RELACIONADA CON LA FQ:Hepatopathy related to cystic fibrosis refers to liver disease that can occur as a complication of cystic fibrosis."}{"title": "INSUFICIENCIA PANCRE\u00c1TICA:INSUFICIENCIA PANCRE\u00c1TICA, or pancreatic insufficiency, is a medical condition characterized by the pancreas's inability to produce sufficient digestive enzymes. This deficiency can lead to impaired nutritional absorption and is commonly associated with several underlying health issues. It is frequently observed in patients with cystic fibrosis, chronic pancreatitis, and liver disease. The lack of adequate enzyme production can significantly affect digestion and overall health, necessitating medical intervention to manage the condition effectively."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD PULMONAR:\"ENFERMEDAD PULMONAR\" refers to a range of conditions that impact the lungs, including Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD), which is recognized as a significant health concern. Additionally, pulmonary disease is a critical component of cystic fibrosis, characterized by chronic inflammation and infection within the lungs. This pulmonary involvement is a common complication in cystic fibrosis, influencing both the management strategies and dietary requirements of affected patients. Overall, pulmonary disease plays a central role in the health challenges faced by individuals with these conditions."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE OBSTRUCCI\u00d3N INTESTINAL DISTAL:Distal Intestinal Obstruction Syndrome (DIOS), also known as \"S\u00edndrome de Obstrucci\u00f3n Intestinal Distal,\" is a significant complication that occurs in patients with cystic fibrosis. This condition is characterized by partial bowel obstruction, which can severely limit oral consumption and overall nutritional intake for affected individuals. DIOS is specifically associated with the complications arising from cystic fibrosis, leading to challenges in managing bowel health and dietary needs."}{"title": "SOBRECRECIMIENTO BACTERIANO:Bacterial overgrowth is a condition that can occur in cystic fibrosis patients due to altered gut flora and digestive issues."}{"title": "ALTERACI\u00d3N DE LA MOTILIDAD INTESTINAL:Altered intestinal motility is a common issue in cystic fibrosis, affecting digestion and nutrient absorption."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULA POLIM\u00c9RICA HC:A specific type of nutritional formula designed for diabetic patients, particularly those with cystic fibrosis."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULA EST\u00c1NDAR:F\u00d3RMULA EST\u00c1NDAR refers to a standard nutritional formula designed for patients who do not have organ failure. This formula is intended to meet general dietary needs and is distinct from specialized formulas that cater to specific medical conditions. It serves as a foundational nutritional option for individuals requiring dietary support without the complexities associated with organ dysfunction."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULA DIABETES:Diabetes formula is a specialized nutritional formula designed to manage blood sugar levels in diabetic patients."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO DE SAN JUAN:The Hospital Universitario de San Juan is a medical facility located in Alicante, Spain, where the patient received treatment for diabetes and abdominal issues."}{"title": "ROSA M\u00aa MIRETE L\u00d3PEZ:Dr. Rosa M\u00aa Mirete L\u00f3pez is a specialist in Endocrinology and Nutrition who treated the patient."}{"title": "SEPTIEMBRE 2017:The month and year when the patient was admitted to the hospital for treatment of an abdominal abscess."}{"title": "ABSCESE ABDOMINAL:An abdominal abscess is a collection of pus that can occur in the abdomen, which was the reason for the patient's urgent admission."}{"title": "FLUIDOTERAPIA ENDOVENOSA:Intravenous fluid therapy is a treatment method used to provide fluids directly into the bloodstream, which was used for the patient during her recovery."}{"title": "TUMORACI\u00d3N ABDOMINAL GIGANTE:The patient presented with a giant abdominal tumor, which was a significant factor in her urgent admission."}{"title": "LAPAROTOM\u00cdA EXPLORADORA:Exploratory laparotomy is a surgical procedure conducted to investigate the underlying causes of a patient's abdominal problems. On March 25, 1998, an exploratory laparotomy was performed, which revealed the presence of neoplasia in the pancreas along with multiple nodules in the liver."}{"title": "SEPSIS GRAVE:Sepsis Grave, or severe sepsis, is a life-threatening condition that occurs when the body's response to an infection leads to significant injury to its own tissues and organs. This serious medical condition can develop as a result of various infections, including peritonitis, which is an inflammation of the peritoneum often caused by bacterial infection. In such cases, the body's overwhelming response to the infection can result in severe complications, making timely medical intervention critical for patient survival."}{"title": "ILEOSTOM\u00cdA TERMINAL:A terminal ileostomy is a surgical procedure that involves creating an opening in the abdominal wall to allow waste to exit the body after the removal of part of the intestine. This procedure is typically performed on patients who experience complications that necessitate such an intervention."}{"title": "ANASTOMOSIS YEYUNOC\u00d3LICA:Yeyuno-colic anastomosis is a surgical procedure performed to connect the jejunum to the colon after resection of the ileum."}{"title": "YEYUNOSTOM\u00cdA DE DESCARGA:The \"YEYUNOSTOM\u00cdA DE DESCARGA\" refers to a jejunostomy procedure specifically designed for decompression. This surgical intervention involves creating an opening in the jejunum to alleviate intestinal obstruction or to manage excessive output from an ileostomy. While the procedure is essential for diverting intestinal contents due to the patient's medical condition, it also carries the risk of leading to nutritional deficiencies. Therefore, careful management of nutrition is crucial following the surgery to ensure the patient's health and well-being."}{"title": "SERVICIO DE CIRUG\u00cdA GENERAL:The General Surgery Service is responsible for the surgical treatment of patients, including those with complex abdominal conditions."}{"title": "E. DE CROHN:E. de Crohn is an inflammatory bowel disease that causes inflammation of the digestive tract, leading to various complications."}{"title": "PERITONITIS FECALOIDEA:Fecaloid peritonitis is an inflammation of the peritoneum caused by the leakage of intestinal contents into the abdominal cavity, often requiring surgical intervention."}{"title": "DRENADO QUIR\u00daRGICO:Surgical drainage is a procedure performed to remove pus or fluid from an abscess, which was done for the patient\u2019s abscess in the right flank."}{"title": "LAPARATOM\u00cdA EXPLORADORA:Exploratory laparotomy is a surgical procedure to open the abdomen and examine the organs, which was performed on the patient to assess her condition."}{"title": "ANASTOMOSIS ILEOTRANSVERSA:Ileotransverse anastomosis is a surgical connection made between the ileum and the transverse colon, which was part of the patient\u2019s surgical treatment."}{"title": "D\u00c9BITO FECALOIDEO:Fecaloid output refers to the discharge of fecal matter from a surgical site, which the patient experienced post-surgery."}{"title": "DRENADO Y DESBRIDAMIENTO:Drainage and debridement are surgical procedures to remove infected tissue and fluid, which were performed on the patient during her treatment."}{"title": "DULAGLUTIDE:Dulaglutide es un medicamento utilizado para el tratamiento de la diabetes en la paciente."}{"title": "GRUPO ANDALUZ DE NUTRICI\u00d3N E INVESTIGACI\u00d3N:Este grupo ha publicado recomendaciones sobre el manejo de la glucemia en pacientes que inician nutrici\u00f3n artificial."}{"title": "CODE\u00cdNA:CODE\u00cdNA is a medication utilized for two primary purposes. Firstly, it is employed in the treatment of diarrhea and is included among the treatment options for patients with FEC (a specific condition). Secondly, CODE\u00cdNA is also used for pain management, as indicated by a patient who is currently taking it for this purpose. This dual functionality highlights CODE\u00cdNA's versatility in addressing both gastrointestinal and pain-related issues."}{"title": "GU\u00cdAS EUROPEAS:The entity \"GU\u00cdAS EUROPEAS\" refers to a set of recommendations aimed at improving the nutritional management of patients, particularly in critical care settings. These guidelines suggest an earlier initiation of parenteral nutrition for critically ill patients, emphasizing the importance of timely nutritional support. Additionally, the European guidelines provide protocols specifically designed for the nutritional management of patients with intestinal disorders, ensuring that these individuals receive appropriate care tailored to their unique needs. Overall, the \"GU\u00cdAS EUROPEAS\" serve as a comprehensive framework for enhancing nutritional strategies in various patient populations."}{"title": "HIDROELECTROL\u00cdTICAS:Hydroelectrolytic alterations refer to imbalances in electrolytes that can occur in patients with intestinal issues."}{"title": "DIARREA SEVERA:Severe diarrhea is a condition that can lead to significant nutritional deficiencies and may require parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS SEMIELEMENTALES:Semi-elemental formulas are specialized nutritional products used for patients with extensive disease affecting absorption."}{"title": "INSULINOTERAPIA:Insulinoterapia, or insulin therapy, is a treatment method that involves the administration of insulin to manage blood glucose levels in patients. This therapy is particularly important for individuals receiving nutritional support and is essential for those with secondary diabetes, especially in cases related to pancreatitis. Additionally, insulin therapy may be necessary for patients with diabetes in the context of pancreatic cancer, highlighting its critical role in managing blood glucose levels in various medical conditions."}{"title": "ESTUDIO STEPS:The STEPS study investigated the effects of teduglutide on patients with short bowel syndrome and their nutritional needs."}{"title": "ADAPTACI\u00d3N INTESTINAL:Intestinal adaptation refers to the process by which the intestine adjusts to changes in nutrition and absorption capabilities."}{"title": "GU\u00cdAS AMERICANAS:GU\u00cdAS AMERICANAS es un conjunto de recomendaciones que establece que no se sugiere la nutrici\u00f3n parenteral en pacientes cr\u00edticos hasta pasados 7-10 d\u00edas."}{"title": "CHRISTIAN SALOM VENDRELL:Dr. Christian Salom Vendrell is a specialist in endocrinology and nutrition at Hospital Universitario Doctor Peset."}{"title": "CARCINOMA EPIDERMOIDE DE LARINGE:Carcinoma epidermoide de laringe is a type of cancer that affects the larynx. It is commonly observed in patients with neoplasms of the head and neck. The patient has been diagnosed with this condition and is currently undergoing treatment for it."}{"title": "GASTROSTOM\u00cdA RADIOL\u00d3GICA PERCUT\u00c1NEA:Gastrostom\u00eda radiol\u00f3gica percut\u00e1nea is a procedure performed on the patient to assist with feeding due to his condition."}{"title": "LARINGUECTOM\u00cdA TOTAL:Laringuectom\u00eda total es una cirug\u00eda que implica la extirpaci\u00f3n completa de la laringe. Este procedimiento se realiza com\u00fanmente en pacientes con c\u00e1ncer de laringe. El paciente est\u00e1 programado para someterse a esta intervenci\u00f3n quir\u00fargica, que es necesaria para tratar la enfermedad."}{"title": "VACIAMIENTO FUNCIONAL DERECHO:Vaciamiento funcional derecho is a surgical procedure related to the patient's cancer treatment."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO DOCTOR PESSET:"}{"title": "GASTROSTOM\u00cdA RADIOLOGICA PERCUT\u00c1NEA:Gastrostom\u00eda radiol\u00f3gica percut\u00e1nea es un procedimiento m\u00e9dico que permite la alimentaci\u00f3n a trav\u00e9s de un tubo insertado en el est\u00f3mago, utilizado en pacientes con dificultades para tragar."}{"title": "AFAGIA:Afagia es la incapacidad para tragar, que puede ser consecuencia de intervenciones quir\u00fargicas o condiciones m\u00e9dicas."}{"title": "SUPLEMENTOS NUTRICIONALES ORALES:Suplementos nutricionales orales son productos dise\u00f1ados para complementar la dieta y proporcionar nutrientes adicionales, utilizados en pacientes con deficiencias nutricionales."}{"title": "CCEE:CCEE, or Consultas Externas Especializadas, refers to specialized medical services that provide care to patients who do not require continuous hospitalization. These services focus on offering specialized follow-up and treatment, ensuring that patients receive the necessary medical attention without the need for an inpatient stay."}{"title": "UN:The UN, in this context, refers to a medical unit that plays a crucial role in the nutritional assessment and treatment of patients, especially in complex cases. Additionally, the UN encompasses the nursing unit responsible for the overall care of the patient, which includes daily wound care and dietary recommendations. This dual focus highlights the UN's commitment to providing comprehensive medical support and specialized nursing care to enhance patient outcomes."}{"title": "GRP:GRP refers to a prophylactic gastrostomy placement that was requested for the patient, serving as a medical intervention to provide nutritional support. This type of feeding tube is utilized for patients who are unable to take food orally, indicating its importance in ensuring adequate nutrition. The gastrostomy route through which the patient received this nutritional support is critical for their recovery post-surgery, highlighting the essential role of GRP in the patient's overall treatment plan."}{"title": "VAR\u00d3N DE 66 A\u00d1OS:The patient is a 66-year-old male who has undergone surgery for laryngeal carcinoma and is receiving nutritional support."}{"title": "TOMOGRAF\u00cdA COMPUTERIZADA:Tomograf\u00eda computerizada (CT) is a diagnostic imaging procedure that revealed the extent of the patient's cancer."}{"title": "AC\u00daFENOS:Ac\u00fafenos refers to the ringing or buzzing in the ears that the patient experienced, prompting further medical evaluation."}{"title": "TOMOGRAF\u00cdA COMPUTERIZADA DE CUELLO:Tomograf\u00eda computerizada de cuello is a diagnostic imaging procedure that revealed the presence of neoplasia and adenopathies in the patient."}{"title": "COMIT\u00c9 DE TUMORES:The Comit\u00e9 de Tumores is a medical committee dedicated to evaluating patients' cases to determine appropriate treatment options for cancer. This committee plays a crucial role in assessing cancer diagnoses and formulating treatment plans, ensuring that patients receive tailored and effective care based on their specific medical needs."}{"title": "CENTRO DE ESPECIALIDADES:"}{"title": "DM:DM refers to diabetes mellitus, a condition that necessitates specific nutritional formulas and insulin management for effective treatment. Additionally, diabetes mellitus complicates the management of patients with rumination syndrome, highlighting the need for careful consideration of both conditions in clinical practice."}{"title": "RT:RT refers to radiotherapy, a treatment that can lead to complications such as mucositis in patients. Additionally, it is noted that the patient underwent RT, which affected their appetite and weight."}{"title": "CDEE:CCEE refers to the outpatient clinic where the patient was monitored after hospital discharge."}{"title": "GLARGINA:Glargina is a type of insulin used for basal insulin therapy in the patient's treatment plan."}{"title": "DIAETA TRITURADA:Dieta triturada refers to the pureed diet recommended for the patient to aid in swallowing and nutrition."}{"title": "DM TIPO 2:DM tipo 2 refers to a patient with Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus who requires specific nutritional formulas."}{"title": "QT:QT refers to chemotherapy, which is also associated with complications in patients requiring nutritional support."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N EN EL PACIENTE ONCOL\u00d3GICO:Nutritional guidelines for oncology patients that include recommendations for managing head and neck neoplasias."}{"title": "NEOPLASIAS DE ORL:"}{"title": "\u00c1NGELA MART\u00cdN PALMERO:Dra. \u00c1ngela Mart\u00edn Palmero is the scientific director and head of the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit at Hospital San Pedro in La Rioja."}{"title": "JULIA OC\u00d3N BRET\u00d3N:Dra. Julia Oc\u00f3n Bret\u00f3n is the scientific director and head of the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit at Hospital Cl\u00ednico Universitario Lozano Blesa in Zaragoza."}{"title": "FENANDO L. CALVO GRACIA:Dr. Fernando L. Calvo Gracia is the author of a clinical case study on nutritional management of a patient with a pancreatic tumor."}{"title": "\u00c1NGELA GONZ\u00c1LEZ D\u00cdAZ-FAES:Dra. \u00c1ngela Gonz\u00e1lez D\u00edaz-Faes is a specialist in Endocrinology and Nutrition at Hospital Universitario Marqu\u00e9s de Valdecilla in Santander. She is also the author of a clinical case study that focuses on nutritional support for a diabetic patient suffering from head and neck cancer."}{"title": "SARA VALLE RODR\u00cdGUEZ-NAVAS:Dra. Sara Valle Rodr\u00edguez-Navas is a specialist in endocrinology and nutrition, dedicated to managing the nutritional care of her patients. She has contributed to the field through her research, notably authoring a clinical case study that focuses on the nutritional management of a patient with type 1 diabetes and rumination syndrome."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL INTERVENTIONS IN HEAD AND NECK CANCER PATIENTS:A narrative review discussing various nutritional interventions for patients undergoing treatment for head and neck cancer."}{"title": "DIABETES MELLITUS AND IMPAIRED GLUCOSE REGULATION IN SPAIN:A study examining the prevalence of diabetes mellitus and impaired glucose regulation in Spain, providing insights into nutritional management for affected patients."}{"title": "ESPEN GUIDELINES ON NUTRITION IN CANCER PATIENTS:Guidelines established by the European Society for Clinical Nutrition and Metabolism (ESPEN) regarding nutritional support for cancer patients."}{"title": "ARGENINE-SUPPLEMENTED NUTRITION IN MALNOURISHED PATIENTS:A clinical study investigating the effects of arginine-supplemented nutrition on long-term survival in malnourished patients with head and neck cancer."}{"title": "SYSTEMATIC REVIEW OF IMMUNONUTRITION:A systematic review analyzing the role of immunonutrition in patients undergoing surgery for head and neck cancer."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL SUPPORT IN CANCER:A comprehensive overview of the role of parenteral and enteral/oral nutritional support in patients with cancer."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL MANAGEMENT IN DIABETIC PATIENTS:A systematic review focusing on enteral nutrition support and the use of diabetes-specific formulas for patients with diabetes.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "HOSPITAL CL\u00cdNICO \"LOZANO BLESA\":Hospital Cl\u00ednico \"Lozano Blesa\" is a medical facility in Zaragoza where Dr. Fernando L. Calvo Gracia works, specializing in endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "TROMBOSIS PORTAL:Trombosis portal es una complicaci\u00f3n que puede presentarse en pacientes con enfermedades hep\u00e1ticas. Esta condici\u00f3n se caracteriza por la formaci\u00f3n de un co\u00e1gulo en la vena porta, lo que puede dar lugar a complicaciones adicionales, como la encefalopat\u00eda hep\u00e1tica. La trombosis portal est\u00e1 estrechamente relacionada con el estado de salud hep\u00e1tico del paciente, lo que resalta la importancia de un manejo adecuado de las enfermedades del h\u00edgado para prevenir esta complicaci\u00f3n."}{"title": "URGENTES:Urgent care visit for bilateral lumbar pain with ureteral irradiation and urinary symptoms without fever on 17/5/97"}{"title": "CIPROFLOXACINO:Ciprofloxacino is a specific quinolone antibiotic primarily used to treat various bacterial infections, including urinary tract infections and acute diarrhea. It is recognized as a basic medication, and its absorption can be enhanced in higher pH conditions, which may be influenced by food intake. Ciprofloxacino is primarily absorbed in the upper digestive tract; however, its absorption can be compromised when administered through a jejunostomy. Additionally, it is utilized in severe cases of inflammatory bowel disease to improve prognosis in situations such as perforation."}{"title": "CARCINOMA INDIFERENCIADO METAST\u00c1SICO DE H\u00cdGADO:Undifferentiated metastatic liver carcinoma of probable endocrine origin diagnosed after biopsy"}{"title": "DTIC:DTIC, also known as Dacarbazine, is a chemotherapy drug utilized in the treatment regimen for patients with cancer. It was initiated as a treatment on February 6, 1998."}{"title": "GAMMAGRAF\u00cdA CON OCTRE\u00d3TIDO:Octreotide scan that showed positive uptake in the head of the pancreas"}{"title": "DUODENOPANCREATECTOM\u00cdA TOTAL:Total duodenopancreatectomy performed on 05/02/1999"}{"title": "CARCINOMA DE P\u00c1NCREAS ENDOCRINO:Endocrine pancreatic carcinoma diagnosed post-surgery"}{"title": "HCD:The right upper quadrant of the abdomen where the patient experienced pain"}{"title": "BILIRRUBINA:Bilirrubina is a substance produced from the breakdown of red blood cells. It plays a crucial role in assessing liver function and hemolysis, as its levels are indicative of these processes. Total bilirubin levels are routinely monitored as part of liver function tests to evaluate the health of the liver and detect any potential issues related to red blood cell breakdown."}{"title": "GOT:Glutamate oxaloacetate transaminase levels were monitored as part of the patient's liver function tests"}{"title": "GPT:Glutamate pyruvate transaminase levels were monitored as part of the patient's liver function tests"}{"title": "GGT:Gamma-glutamyl transferase levels were monitored as part of the patient's liver function tests"}{"title": "CABEZAPANCRE\u00c1TICA:Cabeza pancre\u00e1tica is a specific anatomical region where a localized low-grade tumor was identified in the patient."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N INTRAHOSPITALARIA:Intrahospital nutrition refers to the nutritional support provided to the patient during their hospital stay, including total parenteral nutrition (TPN)."}{"title": "IFN:Interferon (IFN) is a treatment administered to the patient to manage their condition, specifically for cancer treatment."}{"title": "5FU:5FU (Fluorouracil) is a chemotherapy medication used in combination with DTIC for treating the patient's cancer."}{"title": "ESTREPTOZOTOCINA:Streptozotocin is a chemotherapy drug used in the patient's treatment plan for managing cancer."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD ESTABLE:The entity \"ENFERMEDAD ESTABLE\" refers to the patient's condition, which has been characterized as stable following treatment. According to the evolution controls conducted up until March 2008, the patient has maintained a stable disease state, with no changes observed in the peripancreatic adenopathies. This indicates that there has been no progression of the disease, affirming the overall stability of the patient's health condition."}{"title": "MAYO 2000:Mayo 2000 marks a follow-up period in the patient's treatment and monitoring process."}{"title": "AGOSTO 2000:Agosto 2000 is a significant time point in the patient's treatment history, particularly regarding imaging results."}{"title": "NECROSIS HEMORR\u00c1GICA:Necrosis hemorr\u00e1gica refers to the tissue death observed in the patient's gallbladder, indicating complications related to their condition."}{"title": "SPLENOMEGALIA:Esplenomegalia congestiva refers to the enlargement of the spleen observed in the patient, which can be associated with various medical conditions."}{"title": "HEPATITIS B:Hepatitis B is a viral infection that primarily affects the liver and can lead to serious health complications. A patient was diagnosed with hepatitis B in March-April of 2005, which complicated their overall health condition. This infection is particularly concerning for individuals with hemochromatosis, as it poses additional risks and can exacerbate liver-related issues. Hepatitis B is known to cause chronic liver disease and is associated with iron overload, making it a significant concern for patients suffering from conditions that affect iron metabolism."}{"title": "EVEROLIMUS:Everolimus is a medication that has been utilized in the treatment of patients with oncological conditions. It serves as a substitute for ciclosporin in certain treatment scenarios, indicating its versatility and importance in managing various health issues."}{"title": "AN\u00c1LOGO DE SOMATOSTATINA:El an\u00e1logo de somatostatina es un tratamiento que el paciente ha estado recibiendo para controlar sus s\u00edntomas y condiciones de salud."}{"title": "ENCEFALOPAT\u00cdA HYPERAMON\u00c9MICA:La encefalopat\u00eda hiperamon\u00e9mica es un diagn\u00f3stico que se le dio al paciente debido a un shunt espont\u00e1neo en el contexto de trombosis portal."}{"title": "FERROPENIA:FERROPENIA refers to iron deficiency, a condition characterized by a lack of iron in the body, which can lead to anemia. This condition is particularly prevalent among women in developing countries and is also common during adolescence, especially in females who experience heavy menstrual losses. The presence of ferropenia was identified during developmental assessments of patients, indicating a significant deficiency of iron."}{"title": "DEFICIT DE ZINC:El d\u00e9ficit de zinc es una alteraci\u00f3n que puede contribuir a la malnutrici\u00f3n en pacientes con enfermedad hep\u00e1tica cr\u00f3nica. En el caso de un paciente espec\u00edfico, se detect\u00f3 el d\u00e9ficit de zinc durante los controles evolutivos, lo que llev\u00f3 a abordar este problema mediante la administraci\u00f3n de suplementos."}{"title": "HEPATOPATHY:Hepatopathy is a liver disease that affects the patient's metabolism and requires a specific diet rich in branched-chain amino acids."}{"title": "LAMIVUDINA:Lamivudina is an antiviral medication included in the patient's treatment regimen."}{"title": "RIFAXIMINA:Rifaximina is an antibiotic used to treat the patient's condition."}{"title": "SPIRONOLACTONE:Spironolactone is a diuretic medication used in the patient's treatment."}{"title": "VITAMINS AND MINERALS:Vitamins and minerals are essential nutrients that play a crucial role in maintaining health and preventing deficiencies. They are particularly important for patients with specific health conditions, such as celiac disease, where monitoring and supplementation may be necessary to correct specific deficits. While vitamins and minerals can support overall health, it is noted that supplementation may not be beneficial for diabetic patients unless they have existing deficiencies. Overall, these nutrients are vital for health maintenance and are often provided as supplements to support patients' well-being."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL ENTERAL SUPPORT:Nutritional enteral support is a specific type of nutritional intervention provided to the patient due to their condition."}{"title": "BIBLIOGRAPHY:The bibliography encompasses a range of clinical guidelines and studies that focus on nutritional support specifically for cancer patients, as well as broader research related to nutrition, health, and disease prevention. This collection serves as a comprehensive resource for understanding the role of nutrition in the context of health and disease management, particularly in oncology."}{"title": "DEPOSICIONES:Deposiciones refer to the patient's bowel movements, which are monitored for normalcy as part of their health assessment."}{"title": "INSUFICIENCIA RESPIRATORIA AGUDA:INSUFICIENCIA RESPIRATORIA AGUDA, or acute respiratory failure, is a serious medical condition characterized by the inability of the respiratory system to maintain adequate gas exchange, leading to critical health issues for the patient. In managing this condition, Oxepa is a nutritional product specifically designed to support patients suffering from acute respiratory failure, providing essential nutrients that may aid in their recovery."}{"title": "ENCEFALOPAT\u00cdA:Encefalopat\u00eda is a neurological condition characterized by brain dysfunction, which can manifest in patients suffering from urea cycle disorders and severe liver disease. This condition is often a result of hyperammonemia, a buildup of ammonia in the blood, which can significantly impact the overall health and level of consciousness of affected individuals. Encefalopat\u00eda encompasses a wide range of brain dysfunctions, highlighting its complexity and the various underlying causes associated with liver disease and metabolic disorders."}{"title": "HYPERKALEMIA:Hyperkalemia is a medical condition characterized by elevated potassium levels in the blood, which can pose significant health risks. In the patient's case, hyperkalemia was noted as a concerning condition. Additionally, hyperkalemia can occur in conjunction with other conditions such as hypoaldosteronism and hyponatremia, indicating a potential interplay between these disorders."}{"title": "EVALUACI\u00d3N AMBULATORIA:Ambulatory evaluation refers to the patient's last outpatient assessment, which took place in November 2015."}{"title": "ALBUMIN:Albumin is a vital protein found in the blood, playing a significant role as a prognostic indicator in various medical contexts, particularly in cancer patients. It is synthesized in the liver, and its levels are closely associated with liver function and nutritional status, especially in patients with cirrhosis. Albumin levels are routinely measured to assess nutritional status and liver function in patients, and they serve as a marker in nutritional assessments to evaluate overall health. In patients with conditions such as ELA (likely referring to a specific medical condition), monitoring albumin levels is crucial, as higher levels are linked to better survival rates. Additionally, albumin levels can indicate nutritional status and are influenced by refeeding in malnourished individuals. Overall, albumin is recognized as a key serum protein that can predict morbidity and mortality, particularly in relation to a patient's nutritional condition."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO MARQU\u00c9S DE VALDECILLA:Hospital Universitario Marqu\u00e9s de Valdecilla is a hospital located in Santander, specializing in various medical fields including endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "CARCINOMA EPIDERMOIDE:Carcinoma epidermoide is a type of cancer diagnosed in the patient, specifically affecting the right hemilangue."}{"title": "MAXILOFACIAL:Maxilofacial refers to the department or specialty that deals with conditions affecting the face, jaws, and neck, where the patient was referred for nutritional evaluation."}{"title": "TAC CUELLO:TAC cuello refers to a CT scan of the neck that was performed to assess the patient's condition and locate the lesion in the tongue."}{"title": "DIETA DIAB\u00c9TICA BLANDA:A soft diabetic diet is a dietary plan designed for individuals with diabetes, which the patient is currently following due to odinophagia and hyporexia."}{"title": "PLIEGUE CUT\u00c1NEO TRICIPITAL:The Pliegue Cut\u00e1neo Tricipital, also known as the Triceps Skinfold, is a measurement utilized to evaluate body fat and nutritional status. This specific skinfold measurement is an important tool in assessing an individual's nutritional health, providing insights into their body composition."}{"title": "HEMIGLOSECTOMY:Hemiglosectomy is a surgical procedure performed on the patient to remove part of the tongue."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL SUPPLEMENT:Nutritional supplements are specialized products, such as Ensure Plus Advance and Fresubin, designed to provide essential nutrients for individuals with specific dietary needs. These supplements are particularly beneficial for patients requiring enhanced caloric and protein intake, including those managing diabetes. They serve to support overall health and nutritional requirements in various medical and dietary contexts."}{"title": "RADIOTHERAPY:Radiotherapy is a treatment method that employs high doses of radiation to effectively kill cancer cells and reduce the size of tumors. This therapeutic approach is often accompanied by side effects, one of which can include diarrhea. In a specific case, a patient underwent radiotherapy consisting of five sessions to address a medical condition, highlighting its application in clinical settings."}{"title": "INSULIN GLARGINE:Insulin glargine is a long-acting insulin used in the management of diabetes, adjusted for the patient's treatment."}{"title": "MAXILOFACIAL CONSULTATION:Maxillofacial consultation refers to the medical evaluation the patient underwent related to their oral and facial health."}{"title": "SUPPLEMENT ORAL:Oral supplements are nutritional products taken by the patient to support dietary needs, specifically for diabetes management."}{"title": "SERVICIO DE NEFROLOG\u00cdA:El servicio de nefrolog\u00eda est\u00e1 involucrado en el seguimiento y tratamiento de la funci\u00f3n renal del paciente, que ha mejorado levemente tras la adecuada hidrataci\u00f3n y cambios nutricionales."}{"title": "DESNUTRICI\u00d3N CAL\u00d3RICO-PROTEICA MODERADA:La desnutrici\u00f3n cal\u00f3rico-proteica moderada es una condici\u00f3n diagnosticada en el paciente, que afecta su salud y requiere intervenci\u00f3n nutricional."}{"title": "IRC ESTADIO 4:La insuficiencia renal cr\u00f3nica (IRC) en estadio 4 es una condici\u00f3n m\u00e9dica diagnosticada en el paciente, que indica un deterioro significativo de la funci\u00f3n renal."}{"title": "NE ESPEC\u00cdFICA PARA DIABETES:La nutrici\u00f3n enteral espec\u00edfica para diabetes es un tipo de soporte nutricional dise\u00f1ado para mejorar el control gluc\u00e9mico en pacientes diab\u00e9ticos."}{"title": "MARCADORES CL\u00cdNICOS:Los marcadores cl\u00ednicos son utilizados en la valoraci\u00f3n nutricional para identificar el grado de desnutrici\u00f3n en pacientes."}{"title": "MARCADORES ANTROPOM\u00c9TRICOS:Los marcadores antropom\u00e9tricos son medidas f\u00edsicas que ayudan a evaluar el estado nutricional de un paciente."}{"title": "PAR\u00c1METROS BIOQU\u00cdMICOS:Los par\u00e1metros bioqu\u00edmicos son an\u00e1lisis de sangre y otros fluidos corporales que desempe\u00f1an un papel fundamental en la evaluaci\u00f3n del estado de salud y nutrici\u00f3n de los pacientes. Estos par\u00e1metros son especialmente cruciales en el seguimiento de aquellos que han sido sometidos a trasplante de c\u00e9lulas hematol\u00f3gicas. Adem\u00e1s, se utilizan como indicadores en la valoraci\u00f3n nutricional, permitiendo una evaluaci\u00f3n m\u00e1s completa del estado de salud de un paciente."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO ARABA:Hospital Universitario Araba is a medical institution located in Vitoria-Gasteiz, specializing in endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "VITORIA-GASTEIZ:Vitoria-Gasteiz is a city in Spain where the Hospital Universitario Araba is located."}{"title": "DM TIPO 1:Diabetes Mellitus Type 1 is a chronic condition that requires lifelong management, including insulin therapy."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE RUMIACI\u00d3N:El s\u00edndrome de rumiaci\u00f3n es un trastorno que se caracteriza por la regurgitaci\u00f3n involuntaria de alimentos. Esta condici\u00f3n puede resultar en p\u00e9rdida de peso y otras complicaciones. El tratamiento del s\u00edndrome de rumiaci\u00f3n puede incluir diversas intervenciones m\u00e9dicas y nutricionales para abordar los s\u00edntomas y mejorar la calidad de vida de quienes lo padecen."}{"title": "GASTROENTEROLOG\u00cdA:Gastroenterolog\u00eda is the branch of medicine dedicated to the study, diagnosis, and treatment of disorders related to the digestive system. This specialty encompasses a wide range of conditions affecting the gastrointestinal tract, including those specific to pediatric patients. The field involves comprehensive medical services that focus on diagnosing and treating various diseases of the digestive system, ensuring that patients receive the necessary care for their gastrointestinal health."}{"title": "PSIQUIATR\u00cdA:PSIQUIATR\u00cdA is a field of medicine that specializes in the diagnosis and treatment of mental health disorders. It plays a crucial role in assessing patients' attitudes towards enteral nutrition, ensuring that mental health considerations are taken into account in the treatment process. Additionally, a medical service within this field evaluated a patient during their admission and determined that there was no psychiatric pathology present. This comprehensive approach highlights the importance of PSIQUIATR\u00cdA in both the assessment and treatment of individuals with mental health concerns."}{"title": "Y DE ROUX:Procedimiento quir\u00fargico propuesto para el paciente debido a la persistencia de sus s\u00edntomas."}{"title": "REGURGITACI\u00d3N POSTPRANDIAL:S\u00edntoma que presenta el paciente, caracterizado por la expulsi\u00f3n de alimentos tras la ingesta."}{"title": "SONDA DE GASTROYEYUNOSTOM\u00cdA:The \"SONDA DE GASTROYEYUNOSTOM\u00cdA\" is a medical device specifically designed for the administration of enteral nutrition. It is utilized in the treatment of patients who require long-term nutritional support. This device plays a crucial role in ensuring that patients receive the necessary nutrients when they are unable to consume food orally."}{"title": "CINITAPRIDA:Medicamento que se prob\u00f3 en el paciente como parte de su tratamiento para la regurgitaci\u00f3n."}{"title": "LEVOSULPIRIDA:Medicamento que se prob\u00f3 en el paciente como parte de su tratamiento para la regurgitaci\u00f3n."}{"title": "SULPIRIDA:Sulpirida is an antipsychotic medication that is primarily used to treat schizophrenia and other mental health disorders. It was tested in a patient as part of their treatment for regurgitation, indicating its potential application beyond its typical use in psychiatric conditions."}{"title": "CLORPROMAZINA:Medicamento que se prob\u00f3 en el paciente como parte de su tratamiento para la regurgitaci\u00f3n."}{"title": "PAROXETINA:Medicamento que se prob\u00f3 en el paciente como parte de su tratamiento para la regurgitaci\u00f3n."}{"title": "SERTRALINA:Medicamento que se prob\u00f3 en el paciente como parte de su tratamiento para la regurgitaci\u00f3n."}{"title": "MIRTAZAPINA:Medicamento que se prob\u00f3 en el paciente como parte de su tratamiento para la regurgitaci\u00f3n."}{"title": "BENZODIAZEPINAS:Benzodiazepinas are a class of medications known for their ability to produce sedative, anxiolytic, and muscle relaxant effects. These medications can have their effects potentiated by alcohol consumption, which may increase the risk of sedation and respiratory depression. Additionally, benzodiazepinas are utilized in the treatment of seizures, particularly in patients with adrenoleucodistrofia, a rare genetic disorder that affects the adrenal glands and the nervous system. Furthermore, benzodiazepinas have been tested in patients as part of their treatment regimen for conditions such as regurgitation, indicating their diverse therapeutic applications."}{"title": "EVOLUCI\u00d3N PONDERAL:La evoluci\u00f3n ponderal se refiere al seguimiento del peso del paciente a lo largo del tiempo, mostrando cambios significativos en su estado nutricional."}{"title": "DIFICULTAD PARA CONSEGUIR UNA RECUPERACI\u00d3N PONDERAL:"}{"title": "GASTROSTOMY:Gastrostomy is a surgical procedure that involves creating an opening in the stomach to provide nutritional support. This procedure entails placing a feeding tube directly into the stomach, allowing for the delivery of food and medications to individuals who may have difficulty eating by mouth. It is primarily used for patients requiring long-term nutritional assistance."}{"title": "YEUJUNOSTOMY:Yeyunostomy is a surgical procedure that connects the stomach to the jejunum for nutritional purposes."}{"title": "PREGABALIN:Pregabalin is a medication used to treat nerve pain and seizures, which the patient is taking for pain management."}{"title": "ACETYL SALICYLIC ACID:Acetyl salicylic acid, commonly known as aspirin, is used by the patient for pain relief."}{"title": "SYNDROME DE RUMIACI\u00d3N:Syndrome de rumiaci\u00f3n is a functional gastrointestinal disorder characterized by the involuntary contraction of abdominal muscles."}{"title": "ROME IV:Rome IV refers to the diagnostic criteria used for functional gastrointestinal disorders, including the syndrome de rumiaci\u00f3n."}{"title": "ICSI:ICSI stands for Intracytoplasmic Sperm Injection, a procedure used in assisted reproductive technology."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULA DE NUTRICI\u00d3N:A specific type of nutritional formula used for enteral feeding, tailored for patients with different dietary needs."}{"title": "INFECCI\u00d3N DEL ESTOMA:An infection that occurs at the site of a stoma, which can be a complication following surgical procedures like gastrostomy."}{"title": "RUMINATION SYNDROME:Rumination syndrome is a poorly understood disorder that is likely underdiagnosed, characterized by the regurgitation of food and its re-chewing or re-swallowing."}{"title": "BACLOFEN:Baclofen is a medication that has shown utility in improving regurgitation associated with rumination syndrome."}{"title": "CEDERHOLM T:Cederholm T is a researcher focused on the study of sarcopenia and its implications for aging and health. Additionally, Cederholm T is one of the authors of the GLIM criteria for the diagnosis of malnutrition, which holds significance in the context of rumination syndrome. This dual involvement highlights Cederholm T's contributions to both the understanding of age-related muscle loss and the assessment of nutritional status in clinical settings."}{"title": "KESSING BF:Kessing BF is an author who contributed to the study of objective manometric criteria for the rumination syndrome."}{"title": "HALLAND M:Halland M is an author who has researched the diagnosis and treatment of rumination syndrome."}{"title": "ELECTROMYOGRAPHY:Electromyography is a diagnostic tool that can be useful in assessing abdominal wall function in patients with rumination syndrome."}{"title": "MANOMETRY:Manometry is a diagnostic test that measures the pressure within the esophagus and can help in diagnosing rumination syndrome."}{"title": "IMPEDANCE:Impedance is a diagnostic technique that can be combined with high resolution manometry to evaluate esophageal conditions."}{"title": "ELECTROMYOGRAPHY OF ABDOMINAL WALL:Electromyography of the abdominal wall is a diagnostic tool that helps assess muscle function in patients with gastrointestinal disorders."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL FORMULAS:Nutritional formulas are specialized dietary products specifically designed to meet the nutritional needs of patients, particularly those with specific health conditions such as diabetes and dietary restrictions. These products provide essential nutrients and are often utilized in clinical settings for patients who may be unable to consume food orally. They are particularly beneficial for individuals with medical needs, including those with diabetes mellitus and rumination syndrome, as they help improve metabolic control. Overall, nutritional formulas serve as a vital resource for ensuring adequate nutrition in patients with various health challenges."}{"title": "HIGH RESOLUTION MANOMETRY:"}{"title": "ADENOCARCINOMA PANCREATICO DUCTAL:Adenocarcinoma pancre\u00e1tico ductal is the most common form of pancreatic cancer, known for its aggressive nature and low survival rates."}{"title": "BICI:BICI is a comprehensive treatment protocol and medical device designed for managing insulin delivery in patients with diabetes, particularly in oncology settings. It stands for \"Infusor subcut\u00e1neo continuo de insulina,\" which translates to a continuous subcutaneous insulin infuser. This device is specifically utilized to assist in the management of severe hypoglycemia in diabetic patients, ensuring a consistent and effective delivery of insulin to maintain optimal blood glucose levels."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME PARANEOPL\u00c1SICO:S\u00edndrome paraneopl\u00e1sico refers to a set of symptoms that occur in patients with cancer, which are not directly related to the local presence of the tumor."}{"title": "CA 19.9:CA 19.9 is a tumor marker that plays a crucial role in the diagnosis and monitoring of treatment for pancreatic cancer. It has a sensitivity and specificity of up to 92%, making it a valuable tool in the clinical assessment of this type of cancer."}{"title": "NM ABDOMINAL:NM abdominal is a medical procedure reserved for difficult cases, cystic neoplasms, and evaluation of bile ducts."}{"title": "PANCREATECTOMY DUODENAL:Pancreatectomy duodenal is a surgical procedure of choice for tumors located in the head of the pancreas."}{"title": "PANCREATECTOMY DISTAL:Pancreatectomy distal is a surgical procedure performed for tumors located in the body and tail of the pancreas."}{"title": "ADENOCARCINOMA OF PANCREAS:Adenocarcinoma of the pancreas is a type of cancer diagnosed in the patient, confirmed by a TAC abdominal scan."}{"title": "RETINOPATHY DIABETIC:Diabetic retinopathy is a complication of diabetes that affects the eyes, diagnosed in the patient."}{"title": "POLYNEUROPATHY DIABETIC:Diabetic polyneuropathy is a complication of diabetes that affects the peripheral nerves, diagnosed in the patient."}{"title": "MICROINFARTO CEREBRAL:Microinfarto cerebral refers to a small stroke that the patient experienced in 2010 without lasting effects."}{"title": "GASTROSCOPIA:Gastroscopy is a medical procedure performed if there is suspicion that a tumor infiltrates the duodenum."}{"title": "COMA HIPOGLUC\u00c9MICO:Coma hipogluc\u00e9mico refers to a severe state of unconsciousness due to extremely low blood sugar levels experienced by the patient."}{"title": "HIPOGLUCEMIAS GRAVES:Graves hypoglycemia refers to severe episodes of low blood sugar that the patient has been experiencing."}{"title": "EVALUACI\u00d3N DE LA COMISI\u00d3N DE TUMORES:Evaluation by the tumor committee is part of the treatment planning for patients with tumors in hospitals."}{"title": "ESTRE\u00d1IMIENTO PERTINAZ:Pertinacious constipation is a severe form of constipation that the patient experienced, which did not respond to usual treatments."}{"title": "ANTICUERPOS ANTIINSULINA:Anti-insulin antibodies are markers that were tested in the patient to assess his diabetes condition."}{"title": "ANTIGAD:Antigad refers to antibodies that were found positive in the patient, indicating an autoimmune response related to diabetes."}{"title": "C-P\u00c9PTIDO:C-peptide is a marker used to assess insulin production in the patient, which was found to be decreased."}{"title": "VARIABILIDAD GLUC\u00c9MICA:VARIABILIDAD GLUC\u00c9MICA refers to the fluctuations in blood sugar levels that a patient experiences, which is significant in the management of diabetes. This concept encompasses the variations in glucose levels over time, highlighting the importance of monitoring these fluctuations for effective diabetes care."}{"title": "ADENOCARCINOMA DE P\u00c1NCREAS:Adenocarcinoma de p\u00e1ncreas es un tipo de c\u00e1ncer que se origina en el p\u00e1ncreas. En este caso, se ha diagnosticado en estadio IV, lo que indica que la enfermedad ha avanzado significativamente y presenta met\u00e1stasis en el h\u00edgado y el bazo. Este tipo de tumor es conocido por su agresividad y se sospecha en pacientes que presentan diabetes de corta evoluci\u00f3n o un empeoramiento de una diabetes preexistente."}{"title": "S. CAPITIS:S. capitis es un tipo de bacteria que fue identificada en hemocultivos positivos durante el tratamiento del paciente, indicando una infecci\u00f3n."}{"title": "LISA MARTIN:Lisa Martin es la autora de las tablas que se utilizan para evaluar el pron\u00f3stico de supervivencia del paciente con adenocarcinoma de p\u00e1ncreas."}{"title": "MARZO 2018:El evento de marzo de 2018 marca el inicio del tratamiento con NAB-Paclitaxel-Gemcitabina para el paciente con adenocarcinoma de p\u00e1ncreas."}{"title": "ABRIL 2018:El evento de abril de 2018 incluye un ingreso del paciente por hemorragia digestiva alta que se resolvi\u00f3 con tratamiento m\u00e9dico."}{"title": "MAYO 2018:El evento de mayo de 2018 se refiere a un nuevo ingreso del paciente por melenas y fiebre, complicaciones de su estado de salud."}{"title": "JUNIO 2018:El evento de junio de 2018 se refiere a la derivaci\u00f3n del paciente a cuidados paliativos y la suspensi\u00f3n de la quimioterapia."}{"title": "20 DE AGOSTO:El evento del 20 de agosto de 2018 marca la fecha de fallecimiento del paciente debido a sepsis."}{"title": "HDA:HDA se refiere a hemorragia digestiva alta, un evento m\u00e9dico que afect\u00f3 al paciente durante su tratamiento."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME CONSTITUCIONAL:El s\u00edndrome constitucional es un conjunto de s\u00edntomas que el paciente experiment\u00f3 durante los seis meses previos a su diagn\u00f3stico de adenocarcinoma de p\u00e1ncreas."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME FEBRIL:El s\u00edndrome febril es un evento que se present\u00f3 en el paciente, requiriendo ingresos hospitalarios para su correcci\u00f3n."}{"title": "HOSPITALIZACIONES:Hospitalizaciones refer to hospital admissions, which can be influenced by various health conditions and management strategies. In this context, hospitalizations occurred primarily due to severe anemia and complications related to the patient's cancer and its treatment. The patient's hospitalizations were brief and specifically aimed at correcting the anemia and managing these complications. Additionally, it is noted that effective management of frailty and sarcopenia can help reduce the need for such hospital admissions."}{"title": "FEBRERO 2018:"}{"title": "2018:The year 2018 is referenced in the context of nutritional interventions and insulin management."}{"title": "2012:The year 2012 is referenced in the context of nutritional interventions and SNO usage."}{"title": "SEPTIEMBRE:Septiembre is a month referenced in the context of insulin management and nutritional interventions."}{"title": "MARZO:Marzo is a month referenced in the context of insulin management and nutritional interventions."}{"title": "JUNIO:Junio is a month referenced in the context of insulin management and nutritional interventions."}{"title": "ONCOL\u00d3GICO:Oncol\u00f3gico refers to the field of oncology, particularly in relation to patient care and nutritional needs."}{"title": "HOSPITALARIO:HOSPITALARIO refers to the hospital setting, particularly focusing on the role of the hospital pharmacist. The hospital pharmacist is a professional who plays a crucial role in managing the interactions between medications and nutrients for patients receiving enteral nutrition. Additionally, within this hospital context, the prevalence of malnutrition among patients is assessed, highlighting the importance of nutritional management in healthcare settings."}{"title": "PANCREATIC CANCER:Pancreatic cancer is a type of cancer that originates in the tissues of the pancreas. It is known for its aggressive nature and poor prognosis, often being diagnosed at an advanced stage. This cancer is frequently associated with cachexia, a syndrome characterized by significant weight loss and muscle wasting, which poses considerable health challenges for affected individuals. Treatment for pancreatic cancer often requires surgical intervention and nutritional support to manage the symptoms and complications associated with the disease. Additionally, studies have explored the relationship between pancreatic cancer and dietary habits, including the potential protective effects of dietary fiber intake. Overall, pancreatic cancer presents a serious health concern with a high mortality rate, necessitating ongoing research and comprehensive treatment strategies."}{"title": "CAQUEXIA CANCEROSA:CAQUEXIA CANCEROSA, also known as cancer cachexia, is a syndrome that manifests as severe body weight loss, muscle mass depletion, and fat loss, frequently observed in patients suffering from advanced cancer. This condition can also arise from chronic enteritis, which may be a consequence of chemotherapy and/or radiotherapy, resulting in significant malnutrition."}{"title": "ADENOCARCINOMA DE P\u00c1NCREAS DUCTAL:Adenocarcinoma de p\u00e1ncreas ductal is a type of cancer that is frequently associated with cachexia, affecting 70-80% of patients and linked to decreased survival and quality of life."}{"title": "NE NORMOCAL\u00d3RICA Y NORMOPROTEICA:Normocaloric and normoproteic nutritional support with soluble fiber was administered to the patient to normalize weight and regulate intestinal rhythm."}{"title": "DIA:Diabetes Mellitus (DM) is a condition that worsened the patient's metabolic control, leading to elevated blood glucose levels."}{"title": "ACETATO DE MEDROXIPROGESTERONA:ACETATO DE MEDROXIPROGESTERONA, also known as medroxyprogesterone acetate, is a medication that serves multiple therapeutic purposes. It is primarily recognized for its ability to improve appetite and reduce weight loss, particularly in patients suffering from conditions such as cancer. Additionally, this medication may antagonize the catabolic effects of cytokines, which are often elevated in such patients, thereby helping to mitigate the adverse effects associated with these inflammatory markers. Overall, ACETATO DE MEDROXIPROGESTERONA plays a significant role in enhancing the quality of life for individuals experiencing appetite loss and weight reduction due to various medical conditions."}{"title": "SNO INMUNOMODULADORA:Immunomodulatory nutritional support was not chosen for the patient, focusing instead on specific nutritional support for diabetes management."}{"title": "SNO ESPEC\u00cdFICA DE DM:Specific nutritional support for diabetes management was recommended, which does not contain omega-3 or nucleotides."}{"title": "HMB:HMB, or \u03b2-hydroxy-\u03b2-methylbutyrate, is a metabolite of the amino acid leucine. It is commonly used as a dietary supplement aimed at improving muscle mass and strength. Research indicates that HMB may help mitigate muscle loss and promote muscle gain, particularly in elderly individuals and patients with various conditions, including those experiencing excessive post-exercise oxygen consumption (EPOC). While HMB has been studied for its potential benefits in enhancing muscle mass and strength, the clarity of its positive effects for generating specific recommendations remains uncertain. Overall, HMB is recognized for its role in influencing muscle mass, especially in the context of resistance training."}{"title": "ANEMIA SEVERA:Severe anemia is a condition that the patient experienced, leading to hospitalizations and impacting overall health."}{"title": "PSICOF\u00c1RMACOS:PSICOF\u00c1RMACOS, or psychopharmaceuticals, are medications commonly employed in the treatment of various psychiatric conditions. They are particularly utilized to address depressive episodes in patients suffering from severe illnesses, such as cancer. Additionally, psychopharmaceuticals play a significant role in the management of eating disorders, helping to alleviate symptoms related to associated psychiatric conditions."}{"title": "HIDALGO M:Hidalgo M es un autor que contribuy\u00f3 a las gu\u00edas de consenso para el diagn\u00f3stico y tratamiento del c\u00e1ncer pancre\u00e1tico en Espa\u00f1a."}{"title": "MELISA HU:Melisa Hu es una autora que ha investigado sobre el c\u00e1ncer y su relaci\u00f3n con la nutrici\u00f3n."}{"title": "SUPLEMENTACI\u00d3N NUTRICIONAL:Suplementaci\u00f3n nutricional es un enfoque utilizado para mejorar el estado nutricional de pacientes con c\u00e1ncer y prevenir la p\u00e9rdida de peso. Este tipo de suplementaci\u00f3n implica proporcionar nutrientes adicionales para apoyar la salud, especialmente en pacientes que tienen necesidades diet\u00e9ticas espec\u00edficas."}{"title": "VASHI P:Vashi P is an author of a study on outcomes of systematic nutritional assessment and medical nutrition therapy in pancreatic cancer."}{"title": "POPIEL B:Popiel B is an author of a study on outcomes of systematic nutritional assessment and medical nutrition therapy in pancreatic cancer."}{"title": "LAMMERSFIELD C:Lammersfield C is an author of a study on outcomes of systematic nutritional assessment and medical nutrition therapy in pancreatic cancer."}{"title": "GUPTA D:Gupta D is a researcher known for significant contributions to the field of oncology, particularly focusing on the quality of life and nutritional outcomes in cancer patients. They have authored a study that examines the outcomes of systematic nutritional assessment and medical nutrition therapy specifically in pancreatic cancer, highlighting the importance of nutrition in the management of this disease."}{"title": "MUELLER T:Mueller T is an author of a study discussing cachexia and pancreatic cancer treatment options."}{"title": "BURMEISTER M:Burmeister M is an author of a study discussing cachexia and pancreatic cancer treatment options."}{"title": "BACHMANN J:Bachmann J is an author who has conducted research on pancreatic cancer, specifically focusing on cachexia, a condition often associated with this disease. In their studies, Bachmann J discusses various treatment options for cachexia and examines its effects on metabolism and weight loss in patients suffering from pancreatic cancer."}{"title": "MARTIGNONI M:Martignoni M is an author of a study discussing cachexia and pancreatic cancer treatment options."}{"title": "DAVIDSON W:Davidson W is an author of a study on weight stabilization and its association with improved survival in unresectable pancreatic cancer."}{"title": "ASH S:Ash S is an author of a study on weight stabilization and its association with improved survival in unresectable pancreatic cancer."}{"title": "CAPRA S:Capra S is a knowledgeable figure in the field of nutrition, recognized for co-authoring a malnutrition screening tool that aids in identifying individuals at risk of malnutrition. Additionally, Capra S has contributed to research on weight stabilization, specifically examining its association with improved survival rates in patients with unresectable pancreatic cancer. This combination of expertise highlights Capra S's significant involvement in both nutritional assessment and cancer-related studies."}{"title": "BAUER J:Bauer J is an author of a study on weight stabilization and its association with improved survival in unresectable pancreatic cancer."}{"title": "CANCER CACHEXIA STUDY GROUP:"}{"title": "ALFONSO CALA\u00d1AS-CONTINENTE:Alfonso Cala\u00f1as-Continente is a medical professional associated with the Unidad de Gesti\u00f3n Cl\u00ednica de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n at Hospital Universitario Reina Sof\u00eda. He specializes in endocrinology and nutrition, with a particular focus on providing nutritional support for oncology patients, especially those undergoing oncological surgery. Dr. Cala\u00f1as-Continente is also dedicated to contributing to the scientific foundations of healthy eating, emphasizing the importance of nutrition in the management and recovery of patients in the oncology field."}{"title": "ANA BARRERA MART\u00cdN:Dr. Ana Barrera Mart\u00edn is a medical professional involved in the study of healthy eating and nutrition."}{"title": "AURA DULCINEA HERRERA MART\u00cdNEZ:Dr. Aura Dulcinea Herrera Mart\u00ednez is a medical professional contributing to the understanding of healthy eating."}{"title": "\u00c1NGEL REBOLLO ROM\u00c1N:Dr. \u00c1ngel Rebollo Rom\u00e1n is a medical professional who has contributed to the scientific understanding of nutrition."}{"title": "GABRIEL OLVEIRA FUSTER:Dr. Gabriel Olveira Fuster is a medical professional specializing in endocrinology and nutrition, with a particular focus on nutritional requirements and diet therapy. He is affiliated with the Hospital Regional Universitario de M\u00e1laga and the Instituto de Investigaci\u00f3n Biom\u00e9dica de M\u00e1laga. In addition to his specialization, Dr. Olveira Fuster is actively involved in providing nutritional support for patients with pulmonary diseases and conducts research related to nutritional requirements. His expertise encompasses both clinical practice and research in the field of nutrition, making him a significant contributor to the understanding and application of dietary therapies in medical settings."}{"title": "MONTSERRAT GONZALO MAR\u00cdN:Dr. Montserrat Gonzalo Mar\u00edn is a medical professional and researcher specializing in nutritional requirements, clinical nutrition, and dietetics. With expertise in these fields, she contributes to the understanding and application of nutrition in clinical settings."}{"title": "CRISTINA PORCA FERN\u00c1NDEZ:Cristina Porca Fern\u00e1ndez is a dietitian and nutritionist affiliated with the Complejo Hospitalario Universitario de Ferrol. In addition to her role at the hospital, she is also recognized as a medical professional who is involved in nutritional labeling, contributing her expertise to the field of nutrition and dietary health."}{"title": "CRISTINA TEJERA P\u00c9REZ:Cristina Tejera P\u00e9rez is a medical professional specializing in endocrinology and nutrition. She works at the Complex University Hospital of Ferrol, where she is involved in the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service. Dr. Tejera P\u00e9rez focuses on nutritional assessment, contributing her expertise to the field of nutrition and its impact on health."}{"title": "ROC\u00cdO VILLAR TAIBO:Dr. Roc\u00edo Villar Taibo is a medical professional specializing in endocrinology and nutrition. She is affiliated with the Endocrinology Service at the Complex University Hospital of Santiago, where she is actively involved in nutritional assessment. Dr. Villar Taibo contributes to the development of guidelines for artificial nutrition and plays a significant role in the treatment of obesity. Her expertise encompasses both the fields of endocrinology and nutrition, highlighting her commitment to improving patient care in these areas."}{"title": "MIGUEL \u00c1NGEL MART\u00cdNEZ OLMOS:Dr. Miguel \u00c1ngel Mart\u00ednez Olmos is a medical professional specializing in endocrinology and nutrition. He focuses on nutritional assessment and is part of the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service at the Complex University Hospital of Santiago."}{"title": "JOS\u00c9 MANUEL GARC\u00cdA ALMEIDA:Dr. Jos\u00e9 Manuel Garc\u00eda Almeida is a distinguished medical professional specializing in endocrinology and clinical nutrition. He serves as the head of the Endocrinology and Clinical Nutrition Service at Hospital Universitario Virgen de la Victoria in M\u00e1laga, Spain. His expertise encompasses dietary planning and nutritional surveys, with a particular focus on providing nutritional support for celiac disease and gluten-controlled diets. Through his work, Dr. Garc\u00eda Almeida plays a vital role in advancing the understanding and management of dietary needs in patients with specific health conditions."}{"title": "M.\u00aa CRISTINA PORCA FERN\u00c1NDEZ:Dr. M.\u00aa Cristina Porca Fern\u00e1ndez is a medical professional specializing in dietary planning and nutritional surveys. She serves as a dietitian-nutritionist at the Complejo Hospitalario Universitario de Ferrol, located in A Coru\u00f1a, Spain."}{"title": "ANA ZUGASTI MURILLO:Ana Zugasti Murillo is a specialist in endocrinology and nutrition, currently working in the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics section of the Complejo Hospitalario de Navarra. As a medical professional, she focuses on hospital diet planning, utilizing her expertise to develop effective dietary strategies for patients."}{"title": "ESTRELLA PETRINA J\u00c1UREGUI:Dr. Estrella Petrina J\u00e1uregui is a medical professional specializing in hospital diet planning. She serves as the head of the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics section at the Complejo Hospitalario de Navarra, where she plays a crucial role in overseeing dietary practices and nutritional care within the hospital setting."}{"title": "\u00c1NGEL REBOLLO ROM(\"ENTITY\":"}{"title": "C\u00d3RDOBA:"}{"title": "SOCIEDADES AMERICANAS DE CARDIOLOG\u00cdA:The American Heart Association provides dietary recommendations to reduce the risk of cardiovascular diseases."}{"title": "SOCIEDADES AMERICANAS DE DIABETES:The American Diabetes Association offers guidelines for dietary practices to manage and prevent diabetes."}{"title": "SOCIEDADES AMERICANAS DE ONCOLOG\u00cdA:The American Society of Clinical Oncology develops dietary recommendations aimed at reducing cancer risk."}{"title": "ALIMENTACI\u00d3N SALUDABLE:\"ALIMENTACI\u00d3N SALUDABLE\" refers to dietary patterns that promote health and prevent chronic diseases. Healthy eating is linked to improved health outcomes and a decreased risk of developing chronic illnesses. This concept emphasizes the importance of making nutritious food choices to enhance overall well-being."}{"title": "ACS:The American Cancer Society (ACS) is an organization focused on cancer research and prevention strategies."}{"title": "ADA:The American Diabetes Association (ADA) is a prominent organization dedicated to diabetes research, education, and advocacy. It plays a crucial role in providing comprehensive information and establishing criteria related to diabetes, including diagnostic blood glucose ranges. The ADA focuses on developing evidence-based recommendations for diabetes care and management, which encompass guidelines for prevention and dietary advice tailored for individuals living with diabetes. Through its efforts, the ADA aims to enhance the understanding and management of diabetes, ultimately improving the quality of life for those affected by the condition."}{"title": "AHA:The AHA, or American Heart Association, is an organization committed to combating heart disease and stroke through extensive research and educational initiatives. It has played a significant role in public health by providing dietary guidelines aimed at promoting heart health. These guidelines were initially issued from 2000 to 2006 and received an update in 2013, reflecting the AHA's ongoing dedication to improving cardiovascular health through informed dietary practices."}{"title": "IOM:The Institute of Medicine (IOM) is an organization that provides expert advice on health and medicine issues."}{"title": "CRUCIFEROUS VEGETABLES:Cruciferous vegetables are a group of vegetables known for their health benefits, particularly in reducing the risk of cardiovascular disease."}{"title": "DYSLIPIDEMIA:Dyslipidemia is a medical condition characterized by abnormal levels of lipids in the blood, which poses a significant risk factor for cardiovascular disease. This condition is often associated with obesity, highlighting the relationship between lipid levels and body weight."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD CEREBROVASCULAR:Enfermedad cerebrovascular se refiere a un grupo de condiciones que afectan el flujo sangu\u00edneo al cerebro, lo que puede resultar en un accidente cerebrovascular o ictus."}{"title": "FRUTAS Y VERDURAS:Frutas y verduras son alimentos de origen vegetal que se asocian con m\u00faltiples beneficios para la salud, incluyendo la reducci\u00f3n del riesgo de enfermedades cr\u00f3nicas."}{"title": "BETA-CAROTENOS:Los beta-carotenos son compuestos que se encuentran en frutas y verduras de color naranja y verde, y se asocian con beneficios para la salud, incluyendo la reducci\u00f3n del riesgo de enfermedades cr\u00f3nicas."}{"title": "VERDURAS:VERDURAS, or vegetables, are essential components of a balanced diet, providing a wealth of vitamins, minerals, and fiber that contribute to overall health. They are generally low in calories and sodium, making them a healthy choice for various dietary needs. Regular consumption of vegetables is associated with a reduced risk of cancer and plays a crucial role in dietary guidelines, particularly for children and heart health, as emphasized in the DASH and Mediterranean diets. \n\nCertain vegetables may contain small amounts of galactose, which should be consumed with caution by individuals with galactosemia. Additionally, vegetables are recommended for their role in preventing kidney stones and promoting hydration and nutrient intake. Leafy greens, in particular, are highlighted for their high calcium content and are encouraged for daily intake.\n\nVegetables are categorized with specific weight measurements for main and side dishes, and they are noted for their low purine content, which can influence uric acid levels. Some vegetables have been linked to lower serum uric acid levels and a decreased risk of hyperuricemia. However, it is advised to eliminate certain vegetables from the diet prior to specific medical tests to avoid false positives.\n\nOverall, VERDURAS are fundamental in the Mediterranean diet and are emphasized in dietary recommendations for their numerous health benefits, including their contributions to cardiovascular health and overall well-being."}{"title": "CRUC\u00cdFERAS:Las verduras cruc\u00edferas son un grupo de vegetales que han sido objeto de investigaci\u00f3n por sus potenciales efectos protectores frente al c\u00e1ncer."}{"title": "DIETA RICA EN FRUTAS Y VERDURAS:Una dieta que incluye un alto consumo de frutas y verduras se asocia con una reducci\u00f3n del riesgo de varios tipos de c\u00e1ncer."}{"title": "C\u00c1NCER DE ES\u00d3FAGO:C\u00e1ncer de es\u00f3fago es una enfermedad que afecta el es\u00f3fago, caracterizada por la formaci\u00f3n de c\u00e9lulas malignas en sus tejidos. Esta neoplasia se asocia con una alta incidencia de malnutrici\u00f3n y p\u00e9rdida de peso en los pacientes, lo que puede llevar a complicaciones graves como la caquexia. A menudo, el c\u00e1ncer de es\u00f3fago es diagnosticado en estadios avanzados y presenta s\u00edntomas como disfagia, que es la dificultad para tragar. El tratamiento de esta enfermedad generalmente requiere un enfoque quir\u00fargico, como la esofagectom\u00eda, as\u00ed como un manejo nutricional especializado para abordar las complicaciones relacionadas con la malnutrici\u00f3n. Adem\u00e1s, se ha observado que un mayor consumo de frutas y verduras puede reducir el riesgo de desarrollar carcinoma epidermoide, una de las formas m\u00e1s comunes de c\u00e1ncer de es\u00f3fago. En resumen, el c\u00e1ncer de es\u00f3fago es una condici\u00f3n grave que no solo afecta la salud f\u00edsica del paciente, sino que tambi\u00e9n requiere un enfoque integral en su tratamiento y manejo nutricional."}{"title": "C\u00c1NCER G\u00c1STRICO:C\u00e1ncer g\u00e1strico, tambi\u00e9n conocido como c\u00e1ncer de est\u00f3mago, es una enfermedad que afecta el est\u00f3mago y se caracteriza por un pron\u00f3stico desfavorable, especialmente en estadios avanzados. Esta enfermedad puede causar p\u00e9rdida de peso y otros s\u00edntomas relacionados con la inflamaci\u00f3n sist\u00e9mica. El c\u00e1ncer g\u00e1strico es un problema de salud significativo, siendo el quinto tipo de c\u00e1ncer m\u00e1s com\u00fan a nivel mundial y la tercera causa principal de mortalidad por c\u00e1ncer, a menudo diagnosticado en etapas tard\u00edas debido a s\u00edntomas no espec\u00edficos.\n\nEl tratamiento del c\u00e1ncer g\u00e1strico puede requerir cirug\u00eda y un tratamiento nutricional espec\u00edfico, incluyendo cuidados postoperatorios para mejorar la recuperaci\u00f3n y reducir complicaciones. Adem\u00e1s, se ha observado que el c\u00e1ncer g\u00e1strico puede afectar el gasto energ\u00e9tico en reposo de los pacientes, lo que resalta la importancia de la nutrici\u00f3n en su manejo.\n\nExisten factores diet\u00e9ticos que pueden influir en el riesgo de desarrollar c\u00e1ncer g\u00e1strico. Se ha sugerido que una mayor ingesta de fibra diet\u00e9tica puede actuar como un eliminador potencial de nitritos, lo que podr\u00eda ayudar a prevenir esta enfermedad. Por otro lado, un alto consumo de nitritos provenientes de la carne roja o procesada se ha relacionado con un mayor riesgo de c\u00e1ncer g\u00e1strico. Asimismo, el consumo de frutas parece estar asociado con una reducci\u00f3n del riesgo de esta enfermedad, lo que sugiere que una dieta equilibrada puede desempe\u00f1ar un papel protector."}{"title": "C\u00c1NCER HEP\u00c1TICO:C\u00e1ncer hep\u00e1tico is a type of liver cancer that has been the subject of various studies, particularly concerning its relationship with dietary factors. Research indicates that a high intake of omega-3 fatty acids may have implications for the risk of developing this cancer. Additionally, a significant inverse association has been observed between fish consumption and the risk of c\u00e1ncer hep\u00e1tico, suggesting that higher fish intake may lower the likelihood of this disease. Furthermore, the consumption of white meat has been noted to potentially reduce the risk of c\u00e1ncer hep\u00e1tico. In contrast, an increase in the intake of vegetables has also been linked to a decreased risk of developing this type of cancer. Overall, dietary choices, including the consumption of fish, white meat, and vegetables, play a crucial role in influencing the risk of c\u00e1ncer hep\u00e1tico."}{"title": "C\u00c1NCER OV\u00c1RICO:C\u00c1NCER OV\u00c1RICO, or ovarian cancer, is a type of cancer that may be influenced by dietary factors, particularly the consumption of cruciferous vegetables. While some evidence suggests that these vegetables could play a role in reducing the risk of ovarian cancer, the findings are inconsistent, indicating that further research is needed to fully understand the relationship between cruciferous vegetable intake and ovarian cancer risk."}{"title": "LINFOMA NO HODGKIN:Linfoma no Hodgkin, also known as Non-Hodgkin lymphoma, is a type of cancer characterized by the abnormal growth of lymphatic cells. Research indicates that the risk of developing Linfoma no Hodgkin may be influenced by dietary factors. Specifically, several meta-analyses have found an association between the consumption of red and processed meats and an increased risk of this type of lymphoma. Conversely, the risk of Linfoma no Hodgkin may be inversely associated with the consumption of fruits and vegetables, suggesting that a diet rich in these foods could potentially lower the risk of developing this cancer."}{"title": "CARNE:CARNE refers to meat, which plays a significant role in dietary practices. While meat consumption, especially red and processed meat, is associated with various health risks, including chronic diseases, it is also recognized as a vital component of dietary recommendations for children. These recommendations highlight the importance of meat in providing essential protein and maintaining nutritional balance in their diets."}{"title": "CARNE ROJA:La carne roja se asocia con un aumento del riesgo de varios tipos de c\u00e1ncer, incluyendo c\u00e1ncer esof\u00e1gico, g\u00e1strico y colorrectal."}{"title": "CARNE PROCESADA:La carne procesada se relaciona con un incremento del riesgo de c\u00e1ncer colorrectal, p\u00e1ncreas, y otros tipos de c\u00e1ncer."}{"title": "NITRITOS:Los nitritos presentes en la carne est\u00e1n asociados con un mayor riesgo de c\u00e1ncer g\u00e1strico y de vejiga."}{"title": "C\u00c1NCER DE VEJIGA:C\u00e1ncer de vejiga is a type of bladder cancer that has been studied for its associations with dietary factors, particularly omega-3 intake. Research indicates that higher consumption of red and processed meats, as well as nitrites, is linked to an increased risk of developing c\u00e1ncer de vejiga."}{"title": "CEREALES INTEGRALES:Cereales integrales, or whole grains, are a vital source of dietary fiber, vitamins, minerals, and phytochemicals, which contribute to improved health and a reduced risk of various diseases. Their consumption has been linked to a lower risk of colorectal cancer and type 2 diabetes, highlighting their anticancer properties. Whole grains are particularly beneficial for cardiovascular health, as they are associated with a decreased risk of cardiovascular disease and related events. They are also a good source of magnesium, especially when the bran is included.\n\nHowever, it is important to note that some whole grain cereals can fragment easily, which may pose a risk for individuals with swallowing difficulties. Additionally, there are concerns regarding the high phosphorus content in certain whole grains, such as brown rice, which can reach up to 40 mg/g. Despite these considerations, the overall health benefits of consuming whole grains are widely recognized, making them a recommended component of a balanced diet."}{"title": "C\u00c1NCER DE VES\u00cdCULA:C\u00e1ncer de ves\u00edcula is a type of cancer that has been associated with dietary habits, including meat consumption."}{"title": "NUECES:Nueces, commonly known as walnuts, are a type of nut that is recognized for their numerous health benefits, particularly for cardiovascular health. They are rich in omega-3 fatty acids, magnesium, and iron, containing 2.3 mg of iron per 100 grams. Regular consumption of nueces has been associated with lower blood pressure and a reduced risk of coronary disease. Despite their health benefits, it is important to consume nueces in moderation due to their high caloric content. These nuts are versatile and often used in snacks and various cooking applications, making them a popular choice for those looking to enhance their diet with nutritious options."}{"title": "C\u00c1NCER PANCRE\u00c1TICO:C\u00e1ncer pancre\u00e1tico, or pancreatic cancer, is a serious type of cancer that has been the subject of various studies exploring its potential links to dietary factors. Research has investigated the relationship between fish consumption and the incidence of pancreatic cancer, although findings may vary. Additionally, the connection between pancreatic cancer and dietary fiber intake, particularly from whole grains, remains inconsistent according to existing studies. This type of cancer is also noted for its impact on patients' metabolic rates, as it can increase resting energy expenditure. Furthermore, it is crucial to consider pancreatic cancer as a possible diagnosis in patients presenting with pancreatitis, especially when the underlying cause is not clearly identified."}{"title": "PISTACHOS:Pistachios are a type of nut that are recognized for their health benefits and nutritional value. They are often recommended as part of a hypocaloric diet due to their low sodium content. Research has shown that pistachios are strongly associated with lower blood pressure, making them a heart-healthy snack option. In terms of nutrition, pistachios provide 7.3 mg of iron per 100 grams, contributing to their status as a nutritious food choice. Additionally, they are commonly consumed as a snack, enjoyed for their unique flavor and texture."}{"title": "PESCADO:PESCADO refers to fish and seafood, which are highly recommended in dietary guidelines due to their numerous health benefits, particularly in relation to cardiovascular health. Fish is recognized as a significant source of omega-3 fatty acids, essential for overall health and particularly beneficial in children's diets. The consumption of PESCADO has been studied for its positive impacts on various health conditions, including cancer and diabetes. Additionally, PESCADO is permitted in diets prior to medical tests, making it a versatile food choice. It is also important to note that while PESCADO is rich in omega-3 fatty acids and protein, it contains phenylalanine, which should be avoided by individuals with phenylketonuria. Furthermore, PESCADO is utilized in some enteral nutrition products, highlighting its role in dietary formulations aimed at providing essential nutrients."}{"title": "ARRITMIAS:Arritmias, or arrhythmias, are irregular heartbeats that can arise as a complication during procedures such as catheter insertion. These conditions represent alterations in the heart's rhythm and can be caused by various issues, including heart problems like cardiopathy related to iron overload. Additionally, it has been suggested that regular consumption of fish oil may help maintain a normal heart rhythm, particularly in cases of atrial fibrillation."}{"title": "\u00c1CIDO EICOSAPENTAENOICO:Eicosapentaenoic acid (EPA), also known as \u00e1CIDO EICOSAPENTAENOICO, is an essential omega-3 fatty acid that offers significant health benefits, particularly for cardiovascular health. It is recognized for its role in reducing inflammation and is often included in various nutritional solutions to support overall well-being."}{"title": "\u00c1CIDO DOCOSAHEXAENOICO:\u00c1cido Docosahexaenoico, commonly known as docosahexaenoic acid (DHA), is an omega-3 fatty acid that plays a crucial role in promoting brain and heart health. It is particularly significant for brain development and function, making it a vital component often included in various nutritional formulations."}{"title": "SUPLEMENTACI\u00d3N DE OMEGA-3:La suplementaci\u00f3n de omega-3 se refiere a la ingesta de \u00e1cidos grasos omega-3 a trav\u00e9s de suplementos, que ha mostrado beneficios modestos en la prevenci\u00f3n de arritmias y otros problemas de salud."}{"title": "ARITMIAS VENTRICULARES:Condici\u00f3n m\u00e9dica que no parece verse afectada por la suplementaci\u00f3n de omega-3, aunque se observa una tendencia beneficiosa en algunos casos."}{"title": "SUPLEMENTACI\u00d3N:The entity \"SUPLEMENTACI\u00d3N\" encompasses the practice of adding essential nutrients to the diet to enhance health and prevent diseases, particularly for individuals at risk of deficiencies. This process is especially important for patients with specific health conditions, such as those in a chronic state of acidosis, who may benefit from calcium and vitamin D supplementation as part of a ketogenic diet. Additionally, supplementation is crucial for patients with dietary restrictions due to conditions like inflammatory bowel disease (EII) and cystic fibrosis, where tailored nutrient additions, including omega-3 fatty acids, sodium, and fatty acids, are necessary to meet their unique dietary needs. Overall, supplementation plays a vital role in supporting the health of individuals with various medical conditions by ensuring they receive adequate nutrients."}{"title": "C\u00c1NCER DE PULM\u00d3N EN MUJERES:Tipo espec\u00edfico de c\u00e1ncer de pulm\u00f3n que puede verse influenciado por el consumo de \u00e1cidos grasos omega-3, con un posible efecto protector en mujeres."}{"title": "C\u00c1NCER DE MAMA EN MUJERES:Tipo de c\u00e1ncer que afecta a las mujeres y que puede ser influenciado por la ingesta de \u00e1cidos grasos omega-3, mostrando una reducci\u00f3n en el riesgo con la suplementaci\u00f3n."}{"title": "PERSONAS DE MEDIANA EDAD:"}{"title": "C\u00c1NCER DE PIEL:C\u00e1ncer de piel is a type of skin cancer that may be influenced by the intake of omega-3 fatty acids."}{"title": "C\u00c1NCER TIROIDEO:C\u00e1ncer tiroideo is a type of thyroid cancer that has been examined for associations with fish and omega-3 fatty acid intake."}{"title": "C\u00c1NCER OVARIO:C\u00e1ncer de ovario is a type of ovarian cancer that has been studied in relation to omega-3 fatty acids."}{"title": "C\u00c1NCER PULM\u00d3N:C\u00e1ncer de pulm\u00f3n is a type of lung cancer that has been investigated for potential dietary influences, including omega-3 fatty acids."}{"title": "BEBIDAS AZUCARADAS:BEBIDAS AZUCARADAS, or sugary drinks, are beverages that contain added sugars. They are associated with an increased risk of metabolic and cardiovascular diseases. Dietary recommendations discourage the consumption of sugary drinks to promote better health outcomes. Furthermore, these drinks are highlighted in dietary guidelines, which advise limiting their intake for health reasons."}{"title": "CITOCINAS PROINFLAMATORIAS:Las citocinas proinflamatorias son prote\u00ednas que se producen en respuesta a la inflamaci\u00f3n, y su incremento se ha asociado con el consumo de bebidas edulcoradas artificialmente."}{"title": "MORTALIDAD CARDIOVASCULAR:MORTALIDAD CARDIOVASCULAR refers to deaths caused by cardiovascular diseases, which encompass a range of heart-related conditions. This type of mortality has been linked to dietary factors, particularly the consumption of salt and trans fats. The relationship between these dietary components and cardiovascular health highlights the significant impact of nutrition on the risk of heart disease and related fatalities."}{"title": "PRODUCTOS L\u00c1CTEOS:PRODUCTOS L\u00c1CTEOS refer to a category of food items derived from milk, which includes products such as milk, cheese, yogurt, and butter. These dairy products are recognized as a primary source of essential nutrients, particularly calcium and vitamin D, which are crucial for children's dietary needs and overall health. They play a significant role in helping individuals meet their recommended intakes of these nutrients.\n\nIn addition to their nutritional benefits, dairy products have been studied for their effects on blood pressure and are associated with dietary quality and cardiovascular risk reduction. However, it is important to note that dairy products, especially in the European diet, can also be significant sources of saturated fat. Overall, while dairy products offer important health benefits, moderation and balance in consumption are key to maintaining a healthy diet."}{"title": "DIETA HIPOS\u00d3DICA:The \"DIETA HIPOS\u00d3DICA\" is a dietary regimen that restricts sodium intake, primarily recommended for patients with specific health conditions such as hypertension. This low-sodium diet aims to control sodium levels in the body, thereby reducing cardiovascular risks and improving arterial health. It is utilized to treat various health conditions by limiting the consumption of sodium, making it an essential dietary approach for individuals needing to manage their sodium intake for better health outcomes."}{"title": "LACTOFERRINA:Lactoferrin is a component of milk that exhibits antioxidant and anti-inflammatory properties, potentially inhibiting cell proliferation."}{"title": "UNESCO:La UNESCO es la organizaci\u00f3n de las Naciones Unidas encargada de promover la educaci\u00f3n, la ciencia y la cultura a nivel mundial. En 2010, la UNESCO inscribi\u00f3 la dieta mediterr\u00e1nea en la Lista Representativa del Patrimonio Cultural Inmaterial de la Humanidad, reconociendo su importancia cultural y su contribuci\u00f3n a la diversidad cultural global."}{"title": "GLUCOSA PLASM\u00c1TICA:La glucosa plasm\u00e1tica es el nivel de az\u00facar en la sangre, que se ve influenciado por la insulina y la vitamina D, y est\u00e1 relacionado con el s\u00edndrome metab\u00f3lico."}{"title": "FUNDACI\u00d3N DIETA MEDITERR\u00c1NEA:Fundaci\u00f3n Dieta Mediterr\u00e1nea is an organization focused on promoting the Mediterranean diet and its health benefits, including cardiovascular health."}{"title": "ESTUDIO PREDIMED:The \"ESTUDIO PREDIMED\" is a multicenter, randomized clinical trial that investigated the effects of the Mediterranean diet on various health outcomes, particularly focusing on cardiovascular health. The study involved over 7,000 adults who were at high risk for cardiovascular disease. It aimed to analyze not only the impact of the Mediterranean diet on cardiovascular events but also its effects on adiposity and cognitive function. The findings from the study suggest that adherence to the Mediterranean diet is associated with a reduction in cardiovascular events, which may also influence the development of dementia. Overall, the ESTUDIO PREDIMED provides significant insights into the health benefits of the Mediterranean diet, particularly in relation to cardiovascular complications and cognitive health."}{"title": "HOMBRES Y MUJERES DE EDAD AVANZADA:Older men and women aged 55 to 80 years with type 2 diabetes and/or multiple cardiovascular risk factors participated in the study."}{"title": "COMPLICACIONES CARDIOVASCULARES:Cardiovascular complications refer to serious health issues related to the heart and blood vessels, which the Mediterranean diet aims to prevent."}{"title": "EXCESO DE PESO:Exceso de peso, or overweight, is a significant risk factor for cardiovascular disease, often linked to dietary habits."}{"title": "TABAQUISMO:"}{"title": "CANCER OF THE COLON:Colon cancer is a type of cancer that affects the large intestine, and higher adherence to the Mediterranean diet has been associated with a lower incidence of this disease."}{"title": "CANCER OF THE LUNG:Lung cancer is a type of cancer that begins in the lungs, and studies suggest that adherence to the Mediterranean diet may lower its incidence."}{"title": "PREDIMED DIABETES:PREDIMED Diabetes is a study that demonstrated the benefits of adherence to a Mediterranean diet in reducing the risk of type 2 diabetes in older adults with high cardiometabolic risk."}{"title": "SOCIETADES AMERICANAS DE DIABETES Y CARDIOLOG\u00cdA:The American Diabetes and Cardiology Societies are organizations that provide guidelines and consensus on diabetes management and cardiovascular health."}{"title": "NUTRIENTES ANTIINFLAMATORIOS:Anti-inflammatory nutrients include fiber, vitamins, minerals, and antioxidants that contribute to reducing inflammation in the body."}{"title": "NUTRIENTES PROINFLAMATORIOS:Pro-inflammatory nutrients include refined sugars, starches, trans fats, and high-calorie density foods that can exacerbate inflammation."}{"title": "ACEITE DE OLIVA VIRGEN EXTRA:ACEITE DE OLIVA VIRGEN EXTRA, or extra virgin olive oil, is an essential component of the Mediterranean diet. It is widely used for both cooking and dressing dishes, and it is renowned for its numerous health benefits. Notably, this type of olive oil is associated with improved cardiovascular health and is recognized for its role in reducing the risk of type 2 diabetes."}{"title": "CIRCUNFERENCIA DE LA CINTURA:Waist circumference is a measure of abdominal fat that can indicate health risks, and it can be reduced through adherence to the Mediterranean diet."}{"title": "ESTUDIO PREDIMED PLUS:El estudio PREDIMED PLUS es un ensayo multic\u00e9ntrico en desarrollo que evaluar\u00e1 el efecto de la dieta mediterr\u00e1nea sobre la p\u00e9rdida de peso y la salud cardiovascular."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD CARDIOMETAB\u00d3LICA:La enfermedad cardiometab\u00f3lica es un factor de riesgo modificable que se ha relacionado con la demencia y otros problemas de salud."}{"title": "POLIFENOLES:POLIFENOLES son compuestos que est\u00e1n bajo evaluaci\u00f3n por su capacidad para prevenir el crecimiento tumoral y sus efectos antiinflamatorios. Estos compuestos antioxidantes se encuentran en la dieta mediterr\u00e1nea y son conocidos por ayudar a reducir la inflamaci\u00f3n."}{"title": "AZ\u00daCARES REFINADOS:Los az\u00facares refinados son nutrientes proinflamatorios que se reducen con la adherencia a la dieta mediterr\u00e1nea."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS DE ALTA DENSIDAD CAL\u00d3RICA:Los alimentos de alta densidad cal\u00f3rica son aquellos que se limitan en la dieta mediterr\u00e1nea para evitar el aumento de peso."}{"title": "SALUD P\u00daBLICA:SALUD P\u00daBLICA encompasses strategies aimed at promoting healthy eating patterns, such as the Mediterranean diet, to enhance the health of the population and safeguard the environment. It refers to the overall health of the community, recognizing that the effects of gastrointestinal symptoms, including diarrhea and constipation, can differ greatly depending on socio-economic factors."}{"title": "WORLD HEALTH ORGANIZATION:The World Health Organization (WHO) is a specialized agency of the United Nations that is responsible for international public health. Its mandate includes the development of guidelines on various aspects of health, including nutrition. The WHO plays a crucial role in coordinating global health efforts and setting standards to improve health outcomes worldwide."}{"title": "CANCER SOCIETY:The American Cancer Society is an organization focused on cancer prevention and research, providing guidelines on nutrition and physical activity."}{"title": "RUEL MT:Ruel MT is a co-author of a study on dietary diversity and child nutritional status, focusing on nutrition and health surveys."}{"title": "FOOTE JA:Foote JA is an author of research on dietary variants and their impact on nutrient adequacy among adults."}{"title": "MURPHY SP:Murphy SP is a co-author of a study discussing dietary variants and their effects on nutrient adequacy."}{"title": "WANG X:Wang X is an author engaged in various research studies focusing on health outcomes related to dietary habits. This includes investigations into urinary excretion and its implications for health, as well as the relationship between fruit consumption and gastric cancer. Additionally, Wang X has contributed to a systematic review that examines the association between fruit and vegetable consumption and mortality rates. Through these studies, Wang X has made significant contributions to understanding the impact of diet on health."}{"title": "ECKEL RH:Eckel RH is a prominent researcher and co-author of the 2013 American Heart Association (AHA) and American College of Cardiology (ACC) guideline on lifestyle management aimed at reducing cardiovascular risk. In addition to being a co-author, Eckel RH also served as a contributor to this important guideline, which provides recommendations for lifestyle changes to help mitigate cardiovascular risk factors."}{"title": "BANTLE JP:Bantle JP is a notable researcher and co-author of the American Diabetes Association's position statement on nutrition recommendations for diabetes. He has made significant contributions to the field through his studies on the metabolic effects of dietary sucrose and fructose in diabetic subjects, enhancing the understanding of how these sugars impact individuals with diabetes."}{"title": "KUSHI LH:Kushi LH is a co-author of the American Cancer Society Guidelines on nutrition and physical activity for cancer prevention."}{"title": "SLAVIN JL:Slavin JL is an author discussing the health benefits of fruits and vegetables in nutrition research."}{"title": "ARIMOND M:"}{"title": "BLOQUE DIETOTERAPIA:BLOQUE DIETOTERAPIA is an organization involved in dietary therapy and research related to health outcomes."}{"title": "TOH JY:Toh JY is a researcher who has contributed to studies on the effects of flavonoids from fruits and vegetables on cardiovascular risk factors."}{"title": "JURASCHEK SP:Juraschek SP is a researcher who conducted a meta-analysis on the effects of vitamin C supplementation on blood pressure."}{"title": "ABURTO NJ:Aburto NJ is a researcher known for conducting systematic reviews on the health effects of lower sodium intake. In addition to this work, Aburto NJ has also studied the impact of increased potassium intake on cardiovascular risk factors and disease. Through these research efforts, Aburto NJ contributes valuable insights into dietary influences on health, particularly concerning sodium and potassium intake."}{"title": "POLLACK R. L.:Pollack R. L. is a researcher who analyzed the effect of green leafy and cruciferous vegetable intake on cardiovascular disease incidence."}{"title": "KAHLON TS:Kahlon TS is a researcher who investigated the impact of steam cooking on the bile acid binding of various vegetables."}{"title": "MIEDEMA MD:Miedema MD is a researcher who studied the association of fruit and vegetable consumption during early adulthood with coronary artery calcium prevalence."}{"title": "DAUCHET L:Dauchet L is a researcher who conducted a meta-analysis on fruit and vegetable consumption and coronary heart disease risk."}{"title": "HE FJ:He FJ is a researcher recognized for his contributions to the field of nutrition and cardiovascular health. He has conducted studies on the effects of salt reduction on blood pressure, highlighting the importance of dietary modifications in managing hypertension. Additionally, He FJ has analyzed the relationship between increased consumption of fruits and vegetables and a reduced risk of coronary heart disease, emphasizing the role of a healthy diet in preventing cardiovascular conditions."}{"title": "OUDE GRIEP LM:Oude Griep LM is a researcher who studied raw and processed fruit and vegetable consumption and its impact on coronary heart disease incidence."}{"title": "HU D:Hu D is a researcher who investigated the relationship between fruit and vegetable consumption and stroke risk."}{"title": "LARSSON SC:Larsson SC is a researcher who conducted a meta-analysis on dietary potassium intake and stroke risk."}{"title": "D'ELIA L:D'Elia L is a researcher who studied potassium intake, stroke, and cardiovascular disease."}{"title": "WENG LC:Weng LC is a researcher who examined the relationship between ischemic stroke risk and folate status."}{"title": "CHEN GC:Chen GC is a researcher and author who has made significant contributions to the field of health and nutrition. He analyzed the relationship between vitamin C intake and stroke risk, providing valuable insights into dietary factors that may influence cardiovascular health. Additionally, Chen GC conducted a meta-analysis on the consumption of fruits and vegetables and its association with the risk of non-Hodgkin's lymphoma, further highlighting the importance of diet in cancer prevention. Through his work, Chen GC has contributed to a better understanding of how dietary choices can impact health outcomes."}{"title": "WANG ZM:Wang ZM is a researcher who conducted a meta-analysis on flavonol intake and stroke risk."}{"title": "THREAPLETON DE:Threapleton DE is a researcher who studied dietary fiber intake and its relationship with the risk of first stroke."}{"title": "BRADBURY KE:Bradbury KE is a researcher who investigated fruit, vegetable, and fiber intake in relation to cancer risk."}{"title": "GEORGE SM:George SM is a researcher who studied fruit and vegetable intake and its association with cancer risk."}{"title": "BOSETTI C:Bosetti C is a researcher who analyzed the relationship between cruciferous vegetables and cancer risk."}{"title": "PAVIA M:Pavia M is a researcher who studied the association between fruit and vegetable consumption and oral cancer risk."}{"title": "CHOI WJ:Choi WJ is a researcher and author who has focused on examining dietary factors and their associated risks related to thyroid health, specifically in the context of thyroid cancer. Through their work, Choi WJ has contributed to the understanding of how diet may influence thyroid conditions and the potential implications for cancer risk."}{"title": "(\"ENTITY\":"}{"title": "ANN ONCOL:Ann Oncol, also known as Annals of Oncology, is a peer-reviewed scientific journal dedicated to the field of oncology. It publishes a wide range of research related to cancer, including studies that explore the relationship between cancer risk and dietary factors, as well as advancements in cancer treatment. The journal serves as a significant resource for professionals in the medical community, contributing to the ongoing discourse and research in oncology."}{"title": "CLIN NUTR RES:Clin Nutr Res is a journal that publishes research on clinical nutrition and its relationship with various health conditions, including cancer."}{"title": "CANCER CAUSES CONTROL:Cancer Causes & Control is a peer-reviewed journal dedicated to the epidemiology and prevention of cancer. It examines the causes of cancer and the various factors that influence cancer risk. The journal has published significant research, including a meta-analysis on the relationship between red and processed meat intake and the risk of esophageal adenocarcinoma, as well as meta-analyses focusing on colorectal cancer risk factors. Through its publications, Cancer Causes & Control contributes valuable insights into understanding and mitigating cancer risks."}{"title": "EUR J CANCER:Eur J Cancer is a journal that publishes research on cancer treatment, prevention, and epidemiology."}{"title": "NUTR CANCER:NUTR CANCER is a journal dedicated to exploring the relationship between nutrition and cancer. It examines how nutritional factors influence cancer outcomes, providing valuable insights into the interplay between dietary habits and cancer progression. The journal serves as a platform for research and discussion on the impact of nutrition on cancer prevention, treatment, and overall patient health."}{"title": "BREAST CANCER RES TREAT:Breast Cancer Res Treat, also known as Breast Cancer Research and Treatment, is a journal dedicated to the publication of research focused on breast cancer treatment, prevention, and outcomes. The journal serves as a platform for disseminating significant findings related to the management of breast cancer, aiming to advance knowledge and improve patient care in this critical area of oncology."}{"title": "DIAGN PATHOL:Diagn Pathol is a journal that publishes research on diagnostic pathology, including studies on cancer."}{"title": "MEDICINE (BALTIMORE):Medicine (Baltimore) is a journal that publishes research on various medical topics, including cancer and nutrition."}{"title": "PILEGGI C:Pileggi C is an author involved in the meta-analysis of observational studies regarding fruit and vegetable consumption and oral cancer."}{"title": "NOBILE CGA:Nobile CGA is an author who co-authored research on dietary factors and their relationship with cancer risk."}{"title": "ANGELILLO IF:Angelillo IF is an author who contributed to studies on dietary factors and cancer risk."}{"title": "KIM J:Kim J is a researcher who has contributed to the field of cancer research, specifically focusing on the relationship between dietary factors and cancer risk. Notably, Kim J is a co-author of a review that examines the impact of dietary factors on the risk of developing thyroid cancer. Through these studies, Kim J aims to enhance the understanding of how diet may influence cancer risk, particularly in relation to thyroid health."}{"title": "TRUONG T:Truong T is an author who studied the role of dietary iodine and cruciferous vegetables in thyroid cancer."}{"title": "BARON-DUBOURDIEU D:Baron-Dubourdieu D is a co-author of the study on dietary iodine and thyroid cancer."}{"title": "ROUGIER Y:Rougier Y is an author involved in the research on dietary factors and thyroid cancer."}{"title": "GUENEL P:Gu\u00e9nel P is a co-author of the study examining dietary factors in thyroid cancer."}{"title": "CLERO E:Cl\u00e9ro E is an author who studied dietary patterns and their relationship with thyroid cancer."}{"title": "DOYON F:Doyon F is a co-author of the case-control study on dietary patterns and thyroid cancer."}{"title": "CHUNGUE V:Chungue V is an author involved in the research on goitrogenic food and thyroid cancer."}{"title": "RACHEDI F:Rach\u00e9di F is a co-author of the study on dietary patterns and thyroid cancer."}{"title": "BOISSIN JL:Boissin JL is an author who contributed to the research on dietary factors and thyroid cancer."}{"title": "SEBBAG J:Sebbag J is a co-author of the study examining dietary patterns and thyroid cancer."}{"title": "BOSSETTI C:Bosetti C is an author who contributed to the pooled analysis of case-control studies of thyroid cancer."}{"title": "NEGRI E:Negri E is a co-author of the pooled analysis of case-control studies related to thyroid cancer."}{"title": "KOLONEL L:Kolonel L is an author involved in the pooled analysis of thyroid cancer studies."}{"title": "RON E:Ron E is a co-author of the pooled analysis of case-control studies of thyroid cancer."}{"title": "FRANCESCHI S:Franceschi S is an author who contributed to the pooled analysis of thyroid cancer studies."}{"title": "PRESTON-MARTIN S:Preston-Martin S is a co-author of the pooled analysis of case-control studies of thyroid cancer."}{"title": "WANG J:Wang J is a co-author of the meta-analysis on fruit and vegetable intake and esophageal cancer."}{"title": "LENG Y:Leng Y is an author involved in the meta-analysis of fruit and vegetable intake and esophageal cancer."}{"title": "LV C:Lv C is a co-author of the meta-analysis on fruit and vegetable intake and esophageal cancer."}{"title": "KUBO A:Kubo A is an author who studied dietary factors and their risks in esophageal adenocarcinoma."}{"title": "CORLEY DA:Corley DA is a co-author of the research on dietary factors and esophageal cancer."}{"title": "JENSEN CD:Jensen CD is an author involved in the study of dietary factors and esophageal cancer."}{"title": "KAUR R:Kaur R is a co-author of the research on dietary factors and esophageal cancer."}{"title": "WANG Q:Wang Q is an author who studied the consumption of fruit and its effect on gastric cancer risk."}{"title": "CHEN Y:Chen Y is a co-author of a study that investigates the relationship between fruit consumption and gastric cancer risk. Additionally, Chen Y is involved in research focusing on dietary habits and their impact on health outcomes. This work highlights Chen Y's contributions to understanding the effects of diet on health, particularly in relation to cancer risk."}{"title": "GONG G:Gong G is a co-author of the study examining fruit consumption and gastric cancer risk."}{"title": "LI G:Li G is an author who contributed to the research on fruit consumption and gastric cancer."}{"title": "LI C:Li C is a co-author of the study on fruit consumption and gastric cancer risk."}{"title": "KUNZMANN AT:Kunzmann AT is an author who studied dietary fiber intake and colorectal cancer risk."}{"title": "COLEMAN HG:Coleman HG is a co-author of the research on dietary fiber and colorectal cancer."}{"title": "HUANG W-Y:Huang W-Y is an author involved in the study of dietary fiber and colorectal cancer."}{"title": "KITAHARA CM:Kitahara CM is a co-author of the research on dietary fiber and colorectal cancer."}{"title": "CANTWELL MM:Cantwell MM is an author who contributed to the study on dietary fiber and colorectal cancer."}{"title": "BERNDT SI:Berndt SI is a co-author of the research on dietary fiber and colorectal cancer."}{"title": "YANG Y:Yang Y is an author who studied the intake of vegetables and its effect on hepatocellular carcinoma risk."}{"title": "ZHANG D:Zhang D is a prominent researcher who has contributed significantly to the field of nutrition and cancer research. They are a co-author of a meta-analysis examining the relationship between vegetable intake and liver cancer, highlighting the potential protective effects of vegetables against this type of cancer. Additionally, Zhang D has been involved in studying the effects of glutamine on cytokine levels in patients undergoing hematopoietic stem cell transplantation, which is crucial for understanding immune responses in these patients. Furthermore, Zhang D has also conducted a meta-analysis focused on the risks associated with red meat consumption and stomach cancer, providing valuable insights into dietary factors that may influence cancer risk. Through these diverse research efforts, Zhang D has made important contributions to the understanding of dietary impacts on cancer."}{"title": "FENG N:Feng N is an author involved in the study of vegetable intake and liver cancer risk."}{"title": "CHEN G:Chen G is a co-author of the research on vegetable intake and liver cancer."}{"title": "ZHANG T:Zhang T is a co-author of the meta-analysis on fruit and vegetable intake and lung cancer."}{"title": "SONG X:Song X is an author involved in the research on fruit and vegetable intake and lung cancer."}{"title": "ZHANG S:Zhang S is a co-author of the study on fruit and vegetable intake and lung cancer risk."}{"title": "VIEIRA AR:Vieira AR is an author who conducted a systematic review on fruits, vegetables, and lung cancer risk."}{"title": "ABAR L:Abar L is a co-author of the systematic review on fruits, vegetables, and lung cancer."}{"title": "VINGELIENE S:Vingeliene S is an author involved in the systematic review on fruits, vegetables, and lung cancer."}{"title": "CHAN DSM:Chan DSM is a co-author of the systematic review on fruits, vegetables, and lung cancer."}{"title": "AUNE D:Aune D is an author who studied the relationship between fruits, vegetables, and breast cancer risk."}{"title": "NAVARRO-ROSENBLATT D:Navarro-Rosenblatt D is a co-author of the systematic"}{"title": "PERICLEOUS M:Pericleous M is an author who contributed to a systematic review on prostate cancer and dietary factors."}{"title": "WHYAND T:Whyand T is an author who contributed to a systematic review on prostate cancer and dietary factors."}{"title": "CAPLIN ME:Caplin ME is an author who contributed to a systematic review on prostate cancer and dietary factors."}{"title": "NUTR METAB:Nutr Metab is a journal that published a systematic review on prostate cancer and dietary factors."}{"title": "LV DB:Lv DB is an author who conducted a meta-analysis on fruits and vegetables consumption and non-Hodgkin's lymphoma risk."}{"title": "PANG Z:Pang Z is an author who conducted a meta-analysis on fruits and vegetables consumption and non-Hodgkin's lymphoma risk."}{"title": "LIU QF:Liu QF is an author who conducted a meta-analysis on fruits and vegetables consumption and non-Hodgkin's lymphoma risk."}{"title": "INT J CANCER:The \"International Journal of Cancer\" (Int J Cancer) is a peer-reviewed medical journal that focuses on publishing research related to cancer and its treatment. Among its notable contributions, the journal has published a meta-analysis examining the relationship between the consumption of fruits and vegetables and the risk of developing non-Hodgkin's lymphoma. This highlights the journal's commitment to disseminating significant findings in the field of oncology and public health."}{"title": "SCHWINGSCHAKL L:Schwingshackl L is an author who conducted a systematic review and meta-analysis on fruit and vegetable consumption and anthropometric changes."}{"title": "HOFFMANN G:Hoffmann G is an author who conducted a systematic review and meta-analysis on fruit and vegetable consumption and anthropometric changes."}{"title": "KALLE-UHLMANN T:Kalle-Uhlmann T is an author who conducted a systematic review and meta-analysis on fruit and vegetable consumption and anthropometric changes."}{"title": "ARREGUI M:Arregui M is an author who conducted a systematic review and meta-analysis on fruit and vegetable consumption and anthropometric changes."}{"title": "BUIJSEE B:Buijsse B is an author known for conducting significant research in the field of nutrition and health. They have carried out a study focusing on the relationship between fruit and vegetable intake and type 2 diabetes, highlighting the importance of dietary habits in managing this condition. Additionally, Buijsse B has conducted a systematic review and meta-analysis that examines the effects of fruit and vegetable consumption on anthropometric changes, further contributing to the understanding of how these dietary factors influence physical health and body measurements. Through these studies, Buijsse B has provided valuable insights into the role of diet in chronic disease prevention and health promotion."}{"title": "BOEING H:Boeing H is an author who conducted a systematic review and meta-analysis on fruit and vegetable consumption and anthropometric changes."}{"title": "KAISER KA:Kaiser KA is an author who conducted a systematic review and meta-analysis on fruit and vegetable intake and weight loss."}{"title": "BROWN AW:Brown AW is an author who conducted a systematic review and meta-analysis on fruit and vegetable intake and weight loss."}{"title": "BOHAN BROWN MM:Bohan Brown MM is an author who conducted a systematic review and meta-analysis on fruit and vegetable intake and weight loss."}{"title": "SHIKANY JM:Shikany JM is an author who conducted a systematic review and meta-analysis on fruit and vegetable intake and weight loss."}{"title": "MATTES RD:Mattes RD is an author who conducted a systematic review and meta-analysis on fruit and vegetable intake and weight loss."}{"title": "ALLISON DB:Allison DB is a researcher and author who has focused on pharmacotherapy for obesity. In addition to her research in this area, she has conducted a systematic review and meta-analysis examining the relationship between fruit and vegetable intake and weight loss. Through her work, Allison DB contributes valuable insights into dietary influences on obesity and effective treatment strategies."}{"title": "CARTER P:Carter P is an author who conducted a systematic review and meta-analysis on fruit and vegetable intake and type 2 diabetes."}{"title": "GRAY LJ:Gray LJ is an author who conducted a systematic review and meta-analysis on fruit and vegetable intake and type 2 diabetes."}{"title": "TROUGHTON J:Troughton J is an author who conducted a systematic review and meta-analysis on fruit and vegetable intake and type 2 diabetes."}{"title": "KHUNTI K:Khunti K is an author who conducted a systematic review and meta-analysis on fruit and vegetable intake and type 2 diabetes."}{"title": "COOPER AJ:Cooper AJ is an author who conducted a study on fruit and vegetable intake and type 2 diabetes."}{"title": "FOROUHI NG:Forouhi NG is an author who conducted a study on fruit and vegetable intake and type 2 diabetes."}{"title": "YE Z:Ye Z is an author who conducted a study on fruit and vegetable intake and type 2 diabetes."}{"title": "ARRIOLA L:Arriola L is an author who conducted a study on fruit and vegetable intake and type 2 diabetes."}{"title": "BALKAU B:Balkau B is an author who conducted a study on fruit and vegetable intake and type 2 diabetes."}{"title": "BATTAGLIA RICHI E:Battaglia Richi E is an author who reviewed health risks associated with meat consumption."}{"title": "BAUMER B:Baumer B is an author who reviewed health risks associated with meat consumption."}{"title": "CONRAD B:Conrad B is an author who reviewed health risks associated with meat consumption."}{"title": "DARIOLI R:Darioli R is an author who reviewed health risks associated with meat consumption."}{"title": "SCHMID A:Schmid A is an author who reviewed health risks associated with meat consumption."}{"title": "KELLER U:Keller U is an author who reviewed health risks associated with meat consumption."}{"title": "INT J VITAM NUTR RES:Int J Vitam Nutr Res is a journal that published a review of health risks associated with meat consumption."}{"title": "MICHA R:Micha R is an author engaged in research focused on dietary habits and their impact on health outcomes. Notably, Micha R conducted a systematic review examining the consumption of red and processed meat and its associated health risks. Through this work, Micha R contributes valuable insights into the relationship between diet and health, particularly concerning the implications of meat consumption."}{"title": "WALLACE SK:Wallace SK is an author who conducted a systematic review on red and processed meat consumption and health risks."}{"title": "MOZAFFARIAN D:Mozaffarian D is an author recognized for his extensive research on the effects of dietary choices on health. He has conducted a systematic review focusing on the health risks associated with the consumption of red and processed meats. Additionally, Mozaffarian D has evaluated the risks and benefits of fish intake, particularly concerning contaminants and their impact on human health. His work also includes significant research on the effects of trans fatty acids, further contributing to the understanding of how various dietary components influence overall health."}{"title": "CIRCULATION:CIRCULATION is a peer-reviewed journal that specializes in cardiovascular medicine, focusing on research related to heart and vascular health. It publishes a wide range of studies, including systematic reviews and original research articles. Notably, CIRCULATION has published research on various topics such as the health risks associated with red and processed meat consumption, as well as the impact of plant seed consumption on cardiovascular health. The journal covers a broad spectrum of cardiovascular health issues, including studies on coronary heart disease and other related diseases, making it a significant resource for advancements in cardiovascular research and medicine."}{"title": "CHOI Y:Choi Y is an author who conducted a meta-analysis on red and processed meat consumption and esophageal cancer risk."}{"title": "SONG S:Song S is an author who conducted a meta-analysis on red and processed meat consumption and esophageal cancer risk."}{"title": "SONG Y:Song Y is an author who conducted a meta-analysis on red and processed meat consumption and esophageal cancer risk."}{"title": "LEE JE:QU X"}{"title": "BEN Q:Ben Q is an author who conducted a meta-analysis on red and processed meat consumption and esophageal squamous cell carcinoma risk."}{"title": "JIANG Y:Jiang Y is an author who conducted a meta-analysis on red and processed meat consumption and esophageal squamous cell carcinoma risk."}{"title": "ANN EPIDEMIOL:Ann Epidemiol is a journal that published a meta-analysis on red and processed meat consumption and esophageal squamous cell carcinoma risk."}{"title": "HUANG W:Huang W is a researcher and author known for significant contributions to the field of health and nutrition. They co-authored a study focusing on glutamine supplementation in hematopoietic stem cell transplantation, exploring its potential benefits in this medical context. Additionally, Huang W conducted a meta-analysis examining the relationship between red and processed meat intake and the risk of esophageal adenocarcinoma, providing valuable insights into dietary impacts on cancer risk. Through these studies, Huang W has contributed to the understanding of both nutritional supplementation and dietary risks in relation to health outcomes."}{"title": "HAN Y:Han Y is a notable author and researcher who has contributed to the field of medical studies. They co-authored a study published in the International Journal of Surgery, which examined the effect of early oral feeding on the short-term outcomes of patients undergoing laparoscopic distal gastrectomy. Additionally, Han Y conducted a meta-analysis investigating the relationship between red and processed meat intake and the risk of esophageal adenocarcinoma. Through these contributions, Han Y has demonstrated a commitment to advancing knowledge in surgical outcomes and cancer risk factors."}∏ˇ0␀␀␀␀␀[␀1␀␀␀␀␀”␀1␀␀␀␀␀{1␀␀␀␀␀!1␀␀␀␀␀≤1␀␀␀␀␀R1␀␀␀␀␀“1␀␀␀␀␀1␀␀␀␀␀≠1␀␀␀␀␀˛1␀␀␀␀␀
